nt(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/7_2.log:721:    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\"key pixels\\\").\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001519_seed218530468_gpt54_high/seed218530468__1__codegen_prompts__8.log:44:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_20\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/1/des.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内部标记像素的颜色，从外部颜色图例中查找对应的填充方向，然后沿该方向将区域内的标记像素拉伸至区域边界。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格左侧有一列垂直排列的两像素图例条目：每条由一个颜色像素（左列）和紧邻其右的箭头方向指示像素（右列）组成。箭头方向指示像素用四种固定颜色编码方向：red 表示向上、blue 表示向下、green 表示向左、yellow 表示向右。\\\\n  - 网格其余区域包含若干由 grey 像素围成的矩形封闭区域（grey 边框宽度为一像素）。\\\\n  - 每个封闭区域内部有恰好一个非 black 非 grey 的标记像素，其颜色与图例左列中的某个颜色一一对应。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 图例和 grey 边框保持不变。\\\\n  - 对每个封闭区域，读取其内部标记像素的颜色，在图例中找到该颜色对应的方向编码。\\\\n  - 从标记像素出发，沿图例指定的方向逐像素绘制该标记颜色，直到碰到 grey 边框像素（不覆盖 grey）为止。\\\\n  - 标记像素本身保留，拉伸路径上的 black 像素被替换为标记颜色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：标记像素的颜色不是直接决定变换行为——它是一个查找键，需要先在外部图例中匹配颜色以获取方向信息，再执行空间填充。解题需要先破解图例的方向编码，再将其应用到每个区域。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：识别网格中由分隔线划分的若干面板，每个面板包含一个形状和一个颜色提示块；将每个面板中的形状复制到相邻面板中，使用目标面板自身的颜色提示块所指定的颜色来重绘该形状。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 一条 magenta 的完整垂直线将网格分成左右两个面板（如有多条分隔线则分成更多面板，但至少两个）。\\\\n  - 每个面板内部有两种前景元素：（1）一个由单一颜色构成的任意连通形状（面积 >= 4 像素）；（2）一个位于面板底部角落的 2x1 颜色提示块（两个像素颜色相同），该颜色与形状颜色不同。\\\\n  - 不同面板中的形状大小不同，颜色各异，提示块颜色也各异。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保留 magenta 分隔线不变。\\\\n  - 对于每一对相邻面板（左面板 A 和右面板 B）：\\\\n    - 将 A 中形状的像素图案（保持形状的相对位置和朝向）复制到 B 中，放置在 B 的形状原来所在的位置（以原形状的左上角 bbox 对齐），用 B 自身的颜色提示块的颜色绘制。\\\\n    - 同理将 B 中的形状复制到 A 中，用 A 自身的提示块颜色绘制。\\\\n  - 原来的形状被清除（替换为 black），提示块保留不变。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：形状在面板间交换位置，但颜色由目标面板的提示块决定而非来源面板。解题者需要同时理解\\\\\\\"形状来源于相邻面板\\\\\\\"和\\\\\\\"颜色来源于本面板提示块\\\\\\\"这两层分离的映射关系。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格中散布着若干成对的同色端点像素，每对端点位于同一行或同一列；根据路径上散布的\\\\\\\"染色种子\\\\\\\"像素的位置，对连线进行分段着色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 若干前景颜色各出现恰好两次，形成成对的单像素端点。同色的两个端点总是处于同一行或同一列（即它们之间的连线是水平或垂直的直线段）。\\\\n  - 在某些端点对之间的直线路径上，存在一个或多个不同颜色的单像素\\\\\\\"染色种子\\\\\\\"。这些种子的颜色既不是 black 也不与该路径端点颜色相同，且每种种子颜色在整个网格中仅出现一次。\\\\n  - 端点对之间的路径上也可能没有种子（此时路径仅用端点自身颜色填充）。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保留所有端点和种子像素不变。\\\\n  - 对每对同色端点，沿它们之间的直线段（水平或垂直）填充所有 black 像素：\\\\n    - 如果路径上没有种子，整条路径用端点颜色填充。\\\\n    - 如果路径上有种子，路径被种子分成若干段。从起始端点（行号或列号较小者）出发到第一个种子之间的段用端点颜色填充；从每个种子到下一个种子（或到终止端点）之间的段用前一个种子的颜色填充。\\\\n  - 不在任何端点对路径上的像素保持不变。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者首先需要识别同色端点配对关系和它们之间的直线路径，然后需要发现路径上的\\\\\\\"种子\\\\\\\"像素不是噪声而是颜色分界标记，它们将连线分段为不同颜色区域。种子充当分隔符而非被连接的对象，这一角色的识别是关键的隐蔽洞见。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格包含若干彩色\\\\\\\"种子\\\\\\\"像素和一组 grey 方块\\\\\\\"容器\\\\\\\"；每个种子沿四个基本方向发射射线直到被容器或边界阻挡，然后根据每个容器被射线击中的情况来决定是否改变容器的颜色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格中散布若干 grey 的 3x3 实心方块（\\\\\\\"容器\\\\\\\"），互不重叠、互不相邻。\\\\n  - 网格中还有若干单像素的彩色\\\\\\\"种子\\\\\\\"（颜色各异，非 black 非 grey），每个种子不与任何容器相邻。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 对每个种子，沿上、下、左、右四个方向发射射线（一像素宽的直线），射线延伸直到碰到容器的边缘像素或网格边界为止。\\\\n  - 射线经过的 black 像素被替换为该种子的颜色（不覆盖容器或其他种子）。\\\\n  - 统计每个容器被多少条不同颜色的射线击中（射线终止于该容器的边缘像素算\\\\\\\"击中\\\\\\\"）。\\\\n  - 如果一个容器被恰好一种颜色的射线击中（无论该颜色击中几次），则该容器的 grey 像素全部替换为击中它的射线颜色。\\\\n  - 如果一个容器被两种或以上不同颜色的射线击中，或者没有被任何射线击中，则容器保持 grey 不变。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：第一层推理是理解种子向四方发射射线的扩展机制；第二层是发现容器变色的条件不是\\\\\\\"被击中就变色\\\\\\\"，而是\\\\\\\"被唯一一种颜色击中才变色\\\\\\\"——多色竞争导致容器保持中立。解题者需要从样例中区分单色击中与多色击中的不同结果来归纳出这一选择性着色规则。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格中有若干带有彩色\\\\\\\"窗户\\\\\\\"的 grey 建筑物矩形和一条水平地面线；将每栋建筑物向下投影到地面线上，投影区域的颜色由该建筑物窗户中出现最多的颜色决定。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格下部有一条完整的水平 maroon 线作为\\\\\\\"地面\\\\\\\"。\\\\n  - 地面线上方散布若干 grey 实心矩形（\\\\\\\"建筑物\\\\\\\"），它们不接触地面线（与地面线之间有 black 间隔），也互不重叠，水平方向上互不交叉。\\\\n  - 每个 grey 矩形内部嵌有若干单像素的彩色\\\\\\\"窗户\\\\\\\"（窗户颜色非 black 非 grey 非 maroon），同一建筑内可能有多种窗户颜色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保留输入中所有像素不变（建筑物、窗户、地面线、背景均保留）。\\\\n  - 对每栋建筑物，统计其内部所有窗户像素的颜色，找到出现次数最多的颜色（保证唯一最多）。\\\\n  - 将该建筑物的水平跨度（左列到右列）向下投影到地面线正上方的区域：从建筑物底边的下一行开始，一直到地面线的上一行为止，将这片矩形区域中的 black 像素替换为该最多窗户颜色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先理解\\\\\\\"建筑物向地面投影\\\\\\\"的空间变换，然后发现投影的颜色不是建筑物自身的 grey，而是取决于内部窗户颜色的统计——出现最多的窗户颜色决定投影色。两层推理（空间投影 + 颜色统计选择）的结合是解题的关键。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格包含若干用不同颜色绘制的矩形框和一组散落的彩色小标记；每个标记的颜色与某个矩形框匹配，标记在框内的相对象限位置决定了框内应填充颜色的象限。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格中有若干由不同颜色像素绘制的空心矩形框（框线宽度一像素，内部为 black），矩形框互不重叠、互不接触。每个矩形框的内部面积至少为 4x4（可被十字分为四个象限）。\\\\n  - 在矩形框外部散布着若干单像素彩色标记。每个标记的颜色与恰好一个矩形框的颜色相同。每个矩形框恰好有一个对应的外部标记。\\\\n  - 每个标记位于其对应矩形框的某一侧（上方、下方、左方或右方）。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保留所有矩形框线不变，保留所有外部标记不变。\\\\n  - 将每个矩形框的内部用一条水平中线和一条垂直中线（均为虚拟线，不实际绘制）划分为四个象限：左上、右上、左下、右下。\\\\n  - 根据标记相对于矩形框的位置确定填充象限：标记在框的左上方→填充左上象限；标记在框的右上方→填充右上象限；标记在框的左下方→填充左下象限；标记在框的右下方→填充右下象限。具体判定方法：比较标记与框中心的相对位置，标记行号小于框中心行号则为\\\\\\\"上\\\\\\\"否则为\\\\\\\"下\\\\\\\"，标记列号小于框中心列号则为\\\\\\\"左\\\\\\\"否则为\\\\\\\"右\\\\\\\"。\\\\n  - 被选中的象限内的 black 像素替换为该矩形框的颜色。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要首先建立标记与矩形框之间的颜色配对关系，然后发现标记的空间位置不只是\\\\\\\"在哪一侧\\\\\\\"这么简单，而是同时编码了行和列两个维度的方向信息——标记相对于框中心的象限位置与框内被填充的象限位置一一对应。颜色匹配是配对层，空间映射是变换层，二者缺一不可。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格顶部有一排彩色像素作为\\\\\\\"颜色序列指令\\\\\\\"，网格中有若干形状相同但旋转角度不同的 grey 对象；根据每个对象的旋转状态，从颜色序列中选取对应位置的颜色来重绘该对象。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格最顶行是一排彩色像素序列（从左到右依次为四种不同颜色，每种占一个像素，左对齐排列，其余为 black），作为\\\\\\\"颜色序列\\\\\\\"。\\\\n  - 网格下方区域散布若干 grey 的 4-连通对象。所有对象具有相同的基础形状（例如一个不对称的 L 形或 T 形），但各自可能经历了 0 度、90 度、180 度或 270 度的旋转。\\\\n  - 基础形状是不对称的，因此四种旋转状态在视觉上可区分。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 颜色序列行保持不变。\\\\n  - 确定所有 grey 对象共享的基础形状。将基础形状的原始朝向定为 0 度（即与网格中某个参照对象一致，参照对象是面积最大的那个或位于最左上角的那个）。\\\\n  - 对每个 grey 对象，判断它相对于基础形状旋转了几个 90 度（0 次、1 次、2 次或 3 次，即顺时针 0°、90°、180°、270°）。\\\\n  - 颜色序列从左到右的第 1、2、3、4 个颜色分别对应旋转 0 次、1 次、2 次、3 次。\\\\n  - 用对应位置的颜色替换该对象的所有 grey 像素。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：所有对象看起来形状各异，但实际上是同一形状的不同旋转。解题者需要先识别这一旋转关系（这要求心理旋转能力），然后发现顶部颜色序列的位置编码了旋转次数。第一层洞见是\\\\\\\"形状相同只是旋转不同\\\\\\\"，第二层是\\\\\\\"旋转次数映射到序列位置\\\\\\\"。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：网格中有若干成对的同形状对象（每对用不同颜色绘制），以及一条分隔线；分隔线同侧的配对对象合并保留，异侧的配对对象中仅保留面积较大者并将其镜像翻转到另一侧。\\\\n\\\\n- `Input structure`：\\\\n  - 背景为 black。\\\\n  - 网格中间有一条完整的水平 azure 分隔线，将网格分为上半区和下半区。\\\\n  - 上下两个半区中各有若干 4-连通单色对象。某些对象在另一半区有一个形状完全相同（可能经过水平或垂直镜像）的配对对象，配对对象的颜色不同但形状全等。\\\\n  - 每个对象最多有一个配对。也可能有些对象没有配对（孤立对象）。\\\\n  - 配对关系通过形状全等来确定（允许镜像和平移，不允许旋转）。\\\\n\\\\n- `Rule`：\\\\n  - 保留 azure 分隔线不变。\\\\n  - 孤立对象（无配对）保持原样不变。\\\\n  - 对于每一对配对对象：如果两者面积不同，保留面积较大的那个在原位不变，删除面积较小的那个（替换为 black），然后将较大者关于 azure 分隔线做上下镜像，镜像副本用较小者的颜色绘制在对应位置。如果两者面积相同，则都保留不变。\\\\n\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要三层推理：（1）通过形状全等（含镜像）识别跨分隔线的配对关系；（2）发现面积比较决定了哪个被保留、哪个被替换；（3）理解替换机制是\\\\\\\"大对象镜像到小对象所在侧，并采用小对象的颜色\\\\\\\"。配对识别、面积比较、镜像+换色三层逻辑依次嵌套。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/10/codegen_prompts/7.md:12:- `description`：网格被分为左右两半，左半部包含若干彩色对象和一条垂直\\\"镜面线\\\"，右半部是左半部的镜像但每个对象缺失了一部分；规则是根据对象的投影高度在一个隐含色序中查找修复颜色，用该颜色填补右侧缺失部分。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/10/codegen_prompts/7.md:23:  - 计算原始对象的投影高度 H（即对象所跨越的行数）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/10/codegen_prompts/7.md:28:- `Key insight`：表面看这是一道简单的镜像补全题，但修复所用的颜色并非对象原色——解题者必须发现投影高度与修复颜色之间的隐含映射关系。这需要先完成镜像匹配（第一层推理），再测量每个对象的投影高度并归纳出色序映射（第二层推理），最后用映射颜色而非原色进行修补（第三层推理）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_053229_seed218530468_gpt54_high_resume/seed218530468__2__codegen_prompts__7.log:20:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"python - <<'PY'\\\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\\\nfiles = [\\\\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py',\\\\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d968ffd4.py',\\\\n'/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f5f939b.py',\\\\n]\\\\nfor path in files:\\\\n    text = Path(path).read_text()\\\\n    print(f'===== {path} =====')\\\\n    for name in ['def main', 'def generate_input']:\\\\n        i = text.find(name)\\\\n        if i < 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        j = text.find('\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ndef ', i + 1)\\\\n        if j < 0:\\\\n            j = len(text)\\\\n        print(text[i:j].rstrip())\\\\n        print()\\\\nPY\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py =====\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\\\n    - Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\\\n    - Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\\\n    - Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\n    - The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\\\n    components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)\\\\n    assert components, \\\\\\\"expected at least one foreground object\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n    for component in components:\\\\n        coords = component[\\\\\\\"coords\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        _r0, c0, _r1, c1 = map(int, component[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"])\\\\n        assert c1 - c0 + 1 >= 2, \\\\\\\"each object must span at least two columns\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n        erase = coords[coords[:, 1] < c0 + 2]\\\\n        out[erase[:, 0], erase[:, 1]] = bg\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (att1, Claude) ---------------\\\\n# Canvas constraints.\\\\nBG = 8\\\\nGRID_SIZE_RANGE = (8, 11)\\\\nMIN_BACKGROUND_FRACTION = 0.50\\\\n# Object sampling constraints.\\\\nOBJECT_COUNT = 4\\\\nFOREGROUND_COLORS = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9]\\\\nSPRITE_WIDTH_RANGE = (2, 6)\\\\nSPRITE_HEIGHT_RANGE = (2, 5)\\\\nSPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE = (4, 14)\\\\nSPRITE_RETRIES = 30\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 4\\\\nSPRITE_SYMMETRY = \\\\\\\"not_symmetric\\\\\\\"\\\\n# Placement and global retry policy.\\\\nPLACEMENT_PADDING = 1\\\\nPLACEMENT_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nGENERATION_RETRIES = 300\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_RETRIES):\\\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\\\n        if result is not None:\\\\n            return result\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\\\\\"Failed to generate input after {GENERATION_RETRIES} attempts\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/d968ffd4.py =====\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Extend each of two aligned rectangular marker objects toward the other, filling half of the gap across the full perpendicular span.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure\\\\n    - A dominant background contains exactly two solid, same-sized monochromatic rectangles.\\\\n    - The rectangles share either the same row span or the same column span, with a background gap between their facing edges.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule\\\\n    - If the rectangles are side-by-side, color the left half of the inter-object gap across every row with the left object's color, and the right half with the right object's color.\\\\n    - If one rectangle is above the other, color the upper half of the gap across every column with the upper object's color, and the lower half with the lower object's color.\\\\n    - When the gap length is odd, leave the center row/column as background.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight\\\\n    - The marker objects are endpoints of an axial corridor; their own size identifies the facing edge, while the filled corridor spans the whole grid perpendicular to that axis.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n    comps = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)\\\\n    assert len(comps) == 2\\\\n    assert all(_is_solid_rect(g, comp) for comp in comps)\\\\n\\\\n    a, b = comps\\\\n    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = a[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    br0, bc0, br1, bc1 = b[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    assert (ar1 - ar0, ac1 - ac0) == (br1 - br0, bc1 - bc0)\\\\n\\\\n    same_rows = (ar0, ar1) == (br0, br1)\\\\n    same_cols = (ac0, ac1) == (bc0, bc1)\\\\n    assert same_rows != same_cols\\\\n\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n    if same_rows:\\\\n        left, right = sorted(comps, key=lambda comp: comp[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][1])\\\\n        _lr0, _lc0, _lr1, lc1 = left[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        _rr0, rc0, _rr1, _rc1 = right[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        gap = rc0 - lc1 - 1\\\\n        assert gap >= 1\\\\n        span = gap // 2\\\\n        out[:, lc1 + 1 : lc1 + 1 + span] = left[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        out[:, rc0 - span : rc0] = right[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    else:\\\\n        top, bottom = sorted(comps, key=lambda comp: comp[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"][0])\\\\n        _tr0, _tc0, tr1, _tc1 = top[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        br0, _bc0, _br1, _bc1 = bottom[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        gap = br0 - tr1 - 1\\\\n        assert gap >= 1\\\\n        span = gap // 2\\\\n        out[tr1 + 1 : tr1 + 1 + span, :] = top[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        out[br0 - span : br0, :] = bottom[\\\\\\\"color\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (att2) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Layout ranges and bounds.\\\\nALIGNMENTS = (\\\\\\\"H\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"V\\\\\\\")\\\\nRECT_PERP_BOUNDS = (1, 4)\\\\nRECT_AXIAL_VALUES = range(1, 3)\\\\nGAP_VALUES = range(6, 17)\\\\nAXIAL_BOUNDS = (14, 22)\\\\nMARGIN = 1\\\\nPALETTE = tuple(range(10))\\\\nMAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\nVALID_AXIAL_GAP_PAIRS = tuple(\\\\n    (rect_axial, gap)\\\\n    for rect_axial in RECT_AXIAL_VALUES\\\\n    for gap in GAP_VALUES\\\\n    if AXIAL_BOUNDS[0] <= 2 * rect_axial + gap + 2 * MARGIN <= AXIAL_BOUNDS[1]\\\\n)\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    for _ in range(MAX_GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\\\n        if grid is not None:\\\\n            return grid\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\"failed to generate valid d968ffd4 input\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/9f5f939b.py =====\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Mark the missing center of each plus-shaped arrangement of four two-pixel bars with yellow.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - The background is the dominant color.\\\\n    - The single foreground color forms isolated 4-connected objects, each a horizontal or vertical two-pixel bar.\\\\n    - Some bars form an implied plus sign: two horizontal bars and two vertical bars around an empty center, with a one-pixel gap between the center and each bar.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - Keep the input unchanged except at implied plus-sign centers.\\\\n    - For every background pixel with foreground bars at offsets 2-3 cells left, right, above, and below, recolor that center yellow.\\\\n    - The one-pixel gaps immediately next to the center in the four cardinal directions must remain background.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\n    - The yellow pixels are not extending a line; they identify the shared missing center where four separated two-pixel bars align as a plus sign.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    assert g.ndim == 2, \\\\\\\"expected a 2D grid\\\\\\\"\\\\n    height, width = g.shape\\\\n    assert height >= 7 and width >= 7, \\\\\\\"grid must be large enough for the plus motif\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\\\n    foreground = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})\\\\n    assert len(foreground) == 1, \\\\\\\"expected exactly one foreground color\\\\\\\"\\\\n    fg = int(foreground[0])\\\\n    assert bg != Color.YELLOW and fg != Color.YELLOW, \\\\\\\"yellow is reserved for output markers\\\\\\\"\\\\n    _assert_two_cell_bars(g, bg, fg)\\\\n\\\\n    centers = [\\\\n        (r, c)\\\\n        for r in range(3, height - 3)\\\\n        for c in range(3, width - 3)\\\\n        if _is_cross_center(g, r, c, bg, fg)\\\\n    ]\\\\n    assert centers, \\\\\\\"expected at least one missing plus center\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n    for r, c in centers:\\\\n        out[r, c] = Color.YELLOW\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas and color bounds.\\\\nGRID_SIZE_MIN = 8\\\\nGRID_SIZE_MAX_EXCLUSIVE = 21\\\\nBACKGROUND_COLOR = 8\\\\nFOREGROUND_COLOR = 1\\\\n\\\\n# Plus motif placement.\\\\nPLUS_COUNT_MIN = 1\\\\nPLUS_COUNT_MAX_EXCLUSIVE = 5\\\\nCENTER_MARGIN = 3\\\\nCENTER_TRIES = 100\\\\n\\\\n# Distractor bar placement.\\\\nDISTRACTOR_RATIO_MIN = 0.2\\\\nDISTRACTOR_RATIO_MAX = 0.6\\\\nDISTRACTOR_RETRY_MULTIPLIER = 20\\\\nNEW_PLUS_SCAN_RADIUS = 3\\\\n\\\\n# Overall generation retries.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\nNEIGHBOR_OFFSETS = ((-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1))\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\\\n        if result is not None:\\\\n            return result\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\\\\\"Failed to generate valid input after {GENERATION_ATTEMPTS} attempts\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001519_seed218530468_gpt54_high/seed218530468__1__codegen_prompts__5.log:38:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_15\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '/\\\\\\\"'^def main/,/''^def /p'\\\\\\\"' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    H, W = g.shape\\\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001519_seed218530468_gpt54_high/seed218530468__1__codegen_prompts__5.log:43:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"规则和识别方案已经定下来：`main()` 通过“整行地面 + 上方非黑非地面连通矩形建筑”来识别对象，`generate_input()` 则显式保证建筑矩形、窗口多数色唯一、以及投影区始终是黑色。接下来先看目标文件是否已存在，再直接写实现。\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:12:- `description`：将每个彩色对象沿其方向标记指示的方向投影，投影长度由网格边缘对应方向的刻度条全局决定。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:19:  - 每个矩形对象的正右方或正下方（不会同时两个方向）紧邻一个 grey 像素作为\\\"方向标记\\\"。方向标记在对象右侧表示向右投影，在对象下方表示向下投影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:22:  - 对于方向标记在右侧的对象：投影方向为向右，投影长度等于 Lh。从该对象的右边缘下一列开始（覆盖方向标记），向右延伸 Lh 个像素，在对象所占的每一行都绘制与该对象同色的投影条。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:23:  - 对于方向标记在下方的对象：投影方向为向下，投影长度等于 Lv。从该对象的下边缘下一行开始（覆盖方向标记），向下延伸 Lv 个像素，在对象所占的每一列都绘制与该对象同色的投影条。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:24:  - 投影不超出网格边界，超出部分截断。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/3/codegen_prompts/2.md:27:- `Key insight`：解题者需要发现三个独立规则并将它们组合：(1) grey 标记决定投影方向，(2) 投影长度不由对象自身属性决定而是由网格边缘的刻度条全局控制，(3) 水平投影读水平刻度、垂直投影读垂直刻度——方向与刻度条之间存在对应关系。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_053115/10_2.log:1770:- `description`：网格被分为左右两半，左半部包含若干彩色对象和一条垂直\\\"镜面线\\\"，右半部是左半部的镜像但每个对象缺失了一部分；规则是根据对象的投影高度在一个隐含色序中查找修复颜色，用该颜色填补右侧缺失部分。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_053115/10_2.log:1781:  - 计算原始对象的投影高度 H（即对象所跨越的行数）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/continue_20260619_053115/10_2.log:1786:- `Key insight`：表面看这是一道简单的镜像补全题，但修复所用的颜色并非对象原色——解题者必须发现投影高度与修复颜色之间的隐含映射关系。这需要先完成镜像匹配（第一层推理），再测量每个对象的投影高度并归纳出色序映射（第二层推理），最后用映射颜色而非原色进行修补（第三层推理）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/17/codegen_prompts/4.md:15:  - 每个箭头沿其指向方向投影到灰色矩形上，确定它标记的是矩形的哪一行或哪一列。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/17/codegen_prompts/4.md:18:- `Key insight`：箭头不是直接指定输出内容，而是通过行列交叉间接定位矩形内的特定单元格——解题者必须先理解箭头的投影关系，再发现同色配对产生坐标，最后推断排序规则。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/8/codegen_prompts/3.md:281:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/8/codegen_prompts/3.md:294:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/8_3.log:2324:- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_210635_seed1155420539_resume_gpt54_xhigh/12_1.log:2196:    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\"key pixels\\\").\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_053229_seed218530468_gpt54_high_resume/seed218530468__9__codegen_prompts__2.log:44:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_19\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed218530468/9/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"2d0172a1\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"209-224\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nConvert a rough nested line drawing into a clean canonical frame-and-dot diagram.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid has one background color and one foreground color.\\\\n- Foreground 4-connected objects are rough closed frames or small filled blobs.\\\\n- Frames may contain other frames/blobs; blobs outside a frame remain outside it.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Detect the containment tree of foreground objects using holes of each frame object.\\\\n- Replace every blob with one foreground pixel.\\\\n- Replace every frame with a rectangular border padded two cells around its direct children.\\\\n- Place siblings by their original row/column overlap and order, with one empty cell between canonical objects.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The exact wobbly geometry is irrelevant; only enclosure plus relative sibling positions define the output.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"aaef0977\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"25-41\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nReplace an orange canvas with concentric Manhattan-distance color rings centered on the lone marker pixel.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid is an orange background with exactly one non-orange marker pixel.\\\\n- The marker color is one of the colors in the fixed non-orange ring cycle.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- The marker location is distance 0 and keeps the marker color.\\\\n- Each step of Manhattan distance away from the marker advances one position\\\\n  through the cycle green, yellow, black, grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, blue.\\\\n- Fill every pixel of the original grid by this distance-indexed cycle.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The output is not copied from existing objects; it is the\\\\ndistance field around the single marker, colored by a cyclic palette that\\\\nexcludes the orange background.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"bc93ec48\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"48-63\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCopy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The dominant color is the background.\\\\n- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\\\\n- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Start from the input unchanged.\\\\n- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\\\\n- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"15660dd6\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"33-54\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCombine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.\\\\n- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\\\n- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,\\\\n  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on\\\\n  the background.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.\\\\n- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.\\\\n- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask\\\\n  background cells as background; separate rebuilt panels with one\\\\n  background column.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\nThe table encodes a colorized stencil per column: the solid panel supplies\\\\nthe paint color and frame label, while the duplicate template panels supply\\\\nthe shape mask.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"d6e50e54\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"8-25\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each maroon marker toward the blue rectangle and recolor the rectangle red.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nA background canvas contains one solid blue rectangular object and several isolated\\\\nmaroon marker pixels. Each marker is horizontally or vertically aligned with the\\\\nrectangle and lies outside it.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nStart with a background canvas, repaint the blue rectangle red, and move each\\\\nmaroon marker straight toward the rectangle along its row or column. Exactly one\\\\nmarker is strictly closer to the rectangle than all others and enters the\\\\nrectangle boundary; every other marker lands in the adjacent exterior cell just\\\\noutside its aligned side.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe single entering marker is the unique global nearest marker to the rectangle,\\\\nnot the nearest marker on each of the four sides.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"342ae2ed\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"34-49\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nDraw the missing diagonal connector segment between each pair of same-color rectangular objects.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid has one dominant background color.\\\\n- Every foreground color appears as exactly two separated solid rectangular 4-connected objects.\\\\n- The two rectangles of each color are diagonally offset with facing corners on a 45-degree line.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Keep all existing rectangles unchanged.\\\\n- For each foreground color, connect the lower facing corner of the upper rectangle to the upper facing corner of the lower rectangle.\\\\n- Paint only the intervening background pixels on that diagonal, excluding the two endpoint pixels already in the rectangles.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- Same-color rectangles define the endpoints; the output completes the open diagonal between their nearest facing corners.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"f0100645\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"51-68\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSlide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.\\\\n- One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.\\\\n- Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Clear the extra objects from their original positions.\\\\n- For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.\\\\n- Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.\\\\n- Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"c9680e90\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"52-67\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each mirrored bottom source pixel to the far end of its trail and redraw the top half as its reflection.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- A solid non-background row separates equal-height top and bottom halves.\\\\n- The top half has one marker color on the background.\\\\n- In the bottom half, exactly one color has positions that mirror the top markers across the separator, and the other color forms trails touching those source pixels.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Identify the bottom source color by reflecting each bottom color into the top half and matching the top marker set.\\\\n- For every bottom source pixel, follow its unique 4-connected trail of the other bottom color to the trail endpoint.\\\\n- Clear the old top markers, bottom sources, and trails; place the source color at each endpoint and place the top marker color at the reflected endpoint.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The top half is only a mirror display of the bottom moving sources; the actual motion is encoded by the trail attached to each bottom source pixel.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"dfadab01\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"79-93\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExpand each colored control pixel into its corresponding fixed 4x4 glyph.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Black background with single-pixel markers in colors 2, 3, 5, and/or 8.\\\\n- Some inputs also show a sample 4x4 glyph in the output color, with a same-rule marker just below-right of the sample.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Replace each marker color by its learned 4x4 glyph: 2->yellow frame, 3->blue ring, 5->pink diagonal blocks, 8->orange X.\\\\n- Paint each glyph with its top-left corner at the marker pixel, clipping at the grid boundary.\\\\n- Remove the sample glyphs and skip their below-right label markers.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The colored pixels are control pixels for a fixed glyph alphabet; non-control sample glyphs are only legend entries, not preserved scene objects.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"581f7754\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"8-22\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color.\\\\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \\\\\\\"marker\\\\\\\" pixel.\\\\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\\\\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\\\\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"b1986d4b\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"19-37\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRender the filled-square object counts as compact nested stacks ordered by count rank.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nA large noisy grid has a dominant background, scattered non-square noise, and\\\\nfilled monochrome square objects. Each square side length has exactly one\\\\nobject color, and side lengths form consecutive sizes.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nIgnore non-square components. If the lowest square in the scene is of the\\\\nsmallest side length, treat that one smallest square as a distractor and do\\\\nnot count it. For count rank k from left to right, create one block from all\\\\nsquare sizes with at least k remaining objects; draw larger squares first and\\\\nsmaller squares over their upper-left corner, then append one background\\\\nseparator column.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe output is a count histogram of square side lengths, but each histogram\\\\nslot is rendered as nested upper-left square masks using the side colors.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"12\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"753ea09b\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"60-79\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFill the small background compartments bounded by the long contour color.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The grid has one dominant background color and two foreground colors.\\\\n- The more frequent foreground color forms long 8-connected contour fragments.\\\\n- The other foreground color is a fixed distractor/obstacle color that partitions\\\\n  the background but is never recolored.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Split the background into 4-connected regions using all foreground pixels as\\\\n  barriers.\\\\n- Keep the two largest background regions as the outside of the contour drawing.\\\\n- Recolor every other background region that touches a long contour component\\\\n  to the contour color; leave all foreground pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\nThe apparent area fill is exactly a component-level fill of bounded background\\\\ncompartments, not a row-wise interpolation between individual contour pixels.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle