gend box.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    H, W = g.shape\\\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/9/codegen_prompts/5.md:199:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/9/codegen_prompts/5.md:212:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/9/codegen_prompts/1.md:12:用网格边缘的彩色刻度尺确定每个内部色块的裁剪窗口，再按刻度尺颜色顺序拼接裁剪结果。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/9/codegen_prompts/1.md:26:- 边缘刻度尺同时充当了色块的寻址索引和输出排列的顺序指令；解题者必须先发现边缘颜色与内部色块颜色的对应关系，再意识到刻度顺序决定了拼接顺序。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__1__codegen_prompts__5.log:24:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/1/des.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内散落碎片的颜色，将该区域的边框重新着色为碎片颜色；同时将碎片本身替换为边框原来的颜色。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干由单一颜色线段围成的封闭矩形边框，每个边框的颜色各不相同。每个边框内部除了黑色背景外，还散落着若干像素碎片，这些碎片的颜色与该边框不同，但与网格中另一个边框的颜色相同。每种碎片颜色在所有边框内部只出现一次（即每个边框内只有一种非背景碎片颜色）。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个封闭矩形边框，找到其内部散落碎片的颜色 C_inner。将该边框的所有边框像素重新着色为 C_inner。同时，将边框内部的碎片像素替换为该边框原来的颜色 C_border。边框内部的背景像素保持黑色不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现边框内碎片颜色与其他边框颜色之间的\\\\\\\"颜色交换\\\\\\\"映射关系，然后理解变换是边框与内部碎片之间的颜色互换——碎片的颜色告诉你边框该变成什么色，而边框的原色则回填到碎片位置上。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：每个带箭头标记的色块沿箭头方向\\\\\\\"印章式\\\\\\\"复制自身，复制次数由该色块内部孔洞的数量决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不接触的单色连通色块（4-连通），每个色块是不规则形状，其中可能包含零个或多个由背景色形成的内部孔洞（被色块像素完全包围的黑色区域）。每个色块的外侧恰好有一个由 red 像素组成的箭头标记，箭头由三个像素构成：一个尖端像素和两个沿对角线分布的翼像素，整体指向上、下、左、右四个方向之一。箭头尖端与色块边缘恰好相邻（4-邻接）。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个色块，数出其内部孔洞的数量 N。沿箭头指向的方向，在色块的前方，以色块自身的外接矩形宽度（或高度，取决于方向）加 1 格间距为步长，连续复制 N 份该色块的完整形状（包括孔洞保持为黑色）。若 N=0，则色块保持原样不复制。箭头标记在输出中被擦除（变为背景色）。色块本身保留在原位。\\\\n- `Key insight`：箭头仅提供复制方向，而复制次数这一关键信息隐藏在色块自身的拓扑结构中——内部孔洞数即为复制份数。解题者需要同时识别方向线索（箭头）和数量线索（孔洞），并理解它们分别控制变换的不同维度。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：将网格中由分隔线划分的若干面板按照隐含的拼图逻辑重新排列，使得相邻面板的边缘花纹能够无缝对接。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格被 grey 色的单像素宽分隔线均匀划分为 m*n 个等大矩形面板（例如 2*3 或 3*3）。每个面板内部包含彩色图案，且每个面板的四条边缘（紧邻分隔线或网格边界的那一行/列像素）上有特定的颜色序列花纹。整个网格中恰好存在唯一一种排列方式，使得每对相邻面板的共享边缘花纹完全一致（即左面板的右边缘与右面板的左边缘像素逐一相同，上面板的下边缘与下面板的上边缘像素逐一相同）。输入中面板的排列是打乱的。\\\\n- `Rule`：找到所有面板的唯一正确排列，使得每对 4-邻接的面板共享边缘花纹完全匹配。将面板按正确顺序重新放入同样大小的网格中，保留 grey 分隔线。面板内容不做任何修改，仅改变其在网格中的位置。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要将每个面板的四条边缘花纹视为\\\\\\\"拼图接口\\\\\\\"，通过逐对匹配边缘花纹来推断正确的空间排列。关键在于识别出边缘花纹是匹配线索，而非面板内部图案——内部图案是干扰项，真正决定排列的是边缘处的颜色序列。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：识别网格中每个\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\"对象发射的十字射线，根据射线交叉点处的叠加规则确定交叉像素的最终颜色，再将每座塔按其实际覆盖的独占射线长度从长到短排序，输出为对应颜色的竖条。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\"，每座塔是一个 3*3 的单色实心方块，颜色各不相同。从每座塔的中心像素出发，向上、下、左、右四个方向发射与塔同色的射线，射线延伸至网格边界。当两条不同颜色的射线在某个像素交叉时，该像素显示为较大面积塔（3*3 方块面积不算，只看射线覆盖的总像素数更多的那座塔）的颜色。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步：为每座塔画出从中心向四个方向延伸到网格边界的十字射线（不覆盖其他塔的 3*3 方块区域，射线遇到其他塔的方块时截断）。第二步：在射线交叉点处，比较两座塔各自的射线总长度（四个方向之和），用射线总长度较长的塔的颜色覆盖交叉像素。第三步：统计每座塔最终独占的射线像素数（被覆盖的不算），按独占数从大到小排序。第四步：输出一个 1*K 的网格（K 为塔的数量），每个像素按排序顺序填入对应塔的颜色。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题需要三层推理——先构建射线并理解交叉处的覆盖规则（射线总长决定优先级），再统计覆盖后的独占像素数，最后将排序结果编码为颜色条。表面上看到的是彩色十字交叉图案，但规则的核心是\\\\\\\"射线长度决定交叉优先级\\\\\\\"这一非显然的叠加逻辑。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：在由彩色路径连接的节点图中，每个节点根据与其相连的路径颜色混合规则变换自身颜色，路径本身则继承其两端节点变换后颜色的选择结果。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个 2*2 的单色实心方块作为\\\\\\\"节点\\\\\\\"，节点颜色各不相同。节点之间通过单像素宽的彩色直线路径（水平或垂直）连接，每条路径有自己的颜色，且路径颜色与其两端节点的颜色都不同。每个节点恰好连接 2 条或 3 条路径。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步——节点变色：对于每个节点，收集与其相连的所有路径的颜色。如果恰好有 2 条路径，节点变为这两条路径中在 ARC 标准色序（Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon）中排位靠前的那个颜色。如果有 3 条路径，节点变为排位居中的那个颜色。第二步——路径变色：每条路径连接两个节点，取两端节点变换后的新颜色——如果两端新颜色相同，路径变为该颜色；如果不同，路径变为两者中色序排位靠后的那个。节点和路径的形状与位置保持不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现节点颜色的变换依赖于路径颜色的某种选择规则（需要从样例中归纳出\\\\\\\"色序排位\\\\\\\"这一隐含排序），然后发现路径的变换又反过来依赖于节点变换后的结果。两步变换形成依赖链——必须先完成所有节点变色，才能确定路径的新颜色，而色序排位规则本身需要从多个样例的对比中归纳得出。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：将每个彩色形状按其\\\\\\\"影子投影\\\\\\\"方向压扁为单像素宽的色条，投影方向由形状内部唯一的标记像素相对于形状重心的位置决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不接触的单色连通形状（4-连通），每个形状内部恰好嵌入一个 red 标记像素（该像素替换了形状原本颜色的一个像素）。形状各自颜色不同且均非 red 或黑色。每个形状的外接矩形不与其他形状重叠。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个形状，找到其外接矩形的几何中心（取外接矩形行范围和列范围的中点）。观察 red 标记像素相对于该中心的方位：若标记在中心的正上方或正下方（同列或偏差不超过1列），则投影方向为垂直方向——将形状沿垂直方向压缩，即统计形状在每一列上是否存在像素，输出为一个水平色条（单像素高），色条放置在形状外接矩形的垂直中心行，色条长度等于形状在水平方向的跨度，每个有像素存在的列着形状色，无像素的列保持黑色。若标记在中心的正左方或正右方（同行或偏差不超过1行），则投影方向为水平方向——将形状沿水平方向压缩，输出为一个竖直色条（单像素宽），放置在外接矩形的水平中心列。red 标记像素在输出中被擦除，原形状的其余像素也被擦除，仅保留投影后的色条。\\\\n- `Key insight`：red 标记看似只是一个位置标注，实则它与形状重心的相对方位编码了投影轴的选择。解题者需要先归纳出\\\\\\\"标记相对于重心的方向决定压缩轴\\\\\\\"这一规律，再理解\\\\\\\"压缩\\\\\\\"操作是将形状沿该轴做列（或行）存在性投影。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：在被色框分隔的子区域中，每个区域内的散点图案需要被\\\\\\\"传送\\\\\\\"到由隐藏配对规则指定的另一个区域，配对规则由框的边长奇偶性决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有偶数个（如 4 个或 6 个）不重叠的单色空心矩形框，每个框的颜色各不相同。每个框内部（框线以内的区域）包含一组由某种非框色、非背景色的颜色绘制的散点图案（连通或不连通均可），不同框内的散点图案颜色也各不相同。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步——框的配对：将所有框按照边长奇偶性分组。具体地，计算每个框的宽度（列数）和高度（行数）。将\\\\\\\"宽为奇、高为奇\\\\\\\"的框归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为偶、高为偶\\\\\\\"的框归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为奇、高为偶\\\\\\\"归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为偶、高为奇\\\\\\\"归为一组。每组内恰好有两个框，它们构成一对。第二步——图案交换：对于配对的两个框 A 和 B，将 A 内部的散点图案（保持相对于 A 框左上角内侧的偏移不变）搬移到 B 的内部（以 B 框左上角内侧为锚点，相同偏移放置），同时将 B 的散点图案搬到 A 内。散点图案保持原来的颜色不变。框本身保持不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：框的配对规则隐藏在框的几何属性中——宽高的奇偶组合将框两两配对。解题者需要先发现\\\\\\\"哪个框的内容去了哪里\\\\\\\"（观察图案的形状在不同框间的交换），再从框的尺寸中归纳出配对依据是宽高奇偶性的组合匹配，最后理解图案是以锚点对齐方式搬移的。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_7.log:868:用网格边缘的彩色刻度尺确定每个内部色块的裁剪窗口，再按刻度尺颜色顺序拼接裁剪结果。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/9_7.log:882:- 边缘刻度尺同时充当了色块的寻址索引和输出排列的顺序指令；解题者必须先发现边缘颜色与内部色块颜色的对应关系，再意识到刻度顺序决定了拼接顺序。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1155420539/9/codegen_prompts/5.md:137:- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__8__codegen_prompts__7.log:9:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_3\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\nfrom arc_utils import bbox_coords, components_mask, crop_bbox, get_bg, label_mask, paste, random_free_location\\\\nimport random\\\\nfrom functools import lru_cache\\\\nfrom itertools import combinations\\\\n\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    H, W = g.shape\\\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return an inclusive randint from a configured (low, high) pair.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return random.randint(bounds[0], bounds[1])\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\\\\ndef _valid_masks(h: int, w: int, area: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return connected masks that span all four sides of the sprite bbox.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    masks = []\\\\n    for cells in combinations(range(h * w), area):\\\\n        mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\\\n        for cell in cells:\\\\n            mask[cell // w, cell % w] = True\\\\n        spans_edges = mask[0, :].any() and mask[-1, :].any() and mask[:, 0].any() and mask[:, -1].any()\\\\n        if not spans_edges:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        _, n = label_mask(mask, connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY)\\\\n        if n == 1:\\\\n            masks.append(mask)\\\\n    return tuple(masks)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _make_sprite(color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample one connected same-color sprite drawn on the background color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    area = _randint(SPRITE_AREA_RANGE)\\\\n    dims = []\\\\n    for h, w in SPRITE_BBOXES:\\\\n        if h * w >= area and _valid_masks(h, w, area):\\\\n            dims.append((h, w))\\\\n    h, w = random.choice(dims)\\\\n    mask = random.choice(_valid_masks(h, w, area))\\\\n    sprite = np.full((h, w), int(bg), dtype=int)\\\\n    sprite[mask] = int(color)\\\\n    return sprite\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _sample_palette() -> tuple[int, list[int], int | None]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Choose background, key colors, and optional distractor color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    colors = list(COLOR_POOL)\\\\n    bg = random.choice(colors)\\\\n\\\\n    k = _randint(KEY_COUNT_RANGE)\\\\n    remaining = [c for c in colors if c != bg]\\\\n    key_colors = random.sample(remaining, k)\\\\n    remaining = [c for c in remaining if c not in key_colors]\\\\n    distractor_color = random.choice(remaining) if remaining and random.random() < DISTRACTOR_PROB else None\\\\n    return bg, key_colors, distractor_color\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _sample_counts(k: int) -> list[int]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample the target outside-component count for each key color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return [_randint(TARGET_COUNT_RANGE) for _ in range(k)]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _legend_shape(k: int, max_count: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return legend height and width for the key count and largest tally.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bh = KEY_ROW_STEP * k + LEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL\\\\n    bw = TALLY_COL_STEP * max_count + LEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL + _randint(LEGEND_SLACK_RANGE)\\\\n    return bh, bw\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _key_row(i: int) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Map a zero-based key index to its row inside the legend/output box.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return KEY_ROW_FIRST + KEY_ROW_STEP * i\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_expected(key_colors: list[int], counts: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Render the black output tally canvas implied by key colors and counts.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    max_count = max(counts)\\\\n    bh, bw = _legend_shape(len(key_colors), max_count)\\\\n\\\\n    expected = np.full((bh, bw), BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\n    for i, (color, count) in enumerate(zip(key_colors, counts)):\\\\n        rr = _key_row(i)\\\\n        for j in range(count):\\\\n            expected[rr, KEY_COLUMN + TALLY_COL_STEP * j] = int(color)\\\\n    return expected\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_legend(shape: tuple[int, int], key_colors: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return a black legend patch with only the key-column pixels filled.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    legend = np.full(shape, BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\n    for i, color in enumerate(key_colors):\\\\n        legend[_key_row(i), KEY_COLUMN] = int(color)\\\\n    return legend\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _new_grid_with_legend(bg: int, legend: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample a grid and paste the legend away from all canvas edges.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, legend.shape)\\\\n    H = _randint(GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE)\\\\n    W = _randint(GRID_WIDTH_RANGE)\\\\n    min_h = bh + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\\\n    min_w = bw + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\\\n    if H < min_h or W < min_w:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), int(bg), dtype=int)\\\\n    r0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, H - bh - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\\\n    c0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, W - bw - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\\\n    paste(grid, legend, r0, c0)\\\\n    return grid\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_sprite_queue(\\\\n    key_colors: list[int],\\\\n    counts: list[int],\\\\n    distractor_color: int | None,\\\\n    bg: int,\\\\n) -> list[np.ndarray]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Create canonical key sprites, optional distractor sprite, and shuffle them.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    sprites = []\\\\n    for color, count in zip(key_colors, counts):\\\\n        sprite = _make_sprite(color, bg)\\\\n        for _ in range(count):\\\\n            sprites.append(sprite.copy())\\\\n    if distractor_color is not None:\\\\n        sprites.append(_make_sprite(distractor_color, bg))\\\\n    random.shuffle(sprites)\\\\n    return sprites\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _place_sprites(grid: np.ndarray, sprites: list[np.ndarray], bg: int) -> None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Paste sprites into random non-touching free locations in queue order.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    for sprite in sprites:\\\\n        sr, sc = random_free_location(\\\\n            grid,\\\\n            sprite,\\\\n            transparent=bg,\\\\n            padding=SPRITE_PADDING,\\\\n            padding_connectivity=SPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY,\\\\n        )\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/16/1.py:152:    - A horizontally dominated pair makes both rooms use vertical stripes; a vertically dominated pair makes both rooms use horizontal stripes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/16/codegen_prompts/1.md:133:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/16/codegen_prompts/1.md:146:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1942:- `description`：将网格中每个彩色区域视为投影源，根据其相邻 grey 标记的位置确定投影方向，向对面的墙壁投射该区域的轮廓阴影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1951:  - 投影方向为光源方向的反方向（即阴影投射到光源对面）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1952:  - 从彩色区域中每个像素出发，沿投影方向逐格前进，直到碰到 maroon 墙壁。将墙壁前最后一个 black 像素着色为该区域的颜色。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1953:  - 这些着色像素沿墙壁排列，形成该区域的\\\"轮廓阴影\\\"——即区域在垂直于投影方向的轴上的投影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1954:  - 如果投影路径上遇到其他彩色像素或其阴影，穿过它们继续前进（不被阻挡）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_1.log:1957:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先建立\\\"grey 标记 = 光源位置\\\"这一映射，再推导出阴影投射到对面墙壁上这一空间关系；最终的阴影不是区域的简单复制，而是区域沿投影方向坍缩到墙壁上的一维轮廓投影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__12__codegen_prompts__1.log:26:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/12/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"409aa875\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"68-81\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.\\\\n- A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.\\\\n- If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).\\\\n- If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"8f3a5a89\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"22-36\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPaint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.\\\\n- A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.\\\\n- Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.\\\\n- Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).\\\\n- Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"4df5b0ae\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"27-41\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPack the colored sprites along the bottom edge from smallest to largest.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several monochrome 4-connected\\\\nforeground sprites; a full-grid one-cell frame may surround the scene.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nRemove any full-grid rectangular frame, sort the remaining sprites by pixel\\\\narea from smallest to largest, and paste their bounding-box sprites left to\\\\nright with each sprite bottom-aligned.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe original locations do not determine the final slots; each sprite's area\\\\ngives the packing order, while its shape and color are preserved.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"a6953f00\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"45-63\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExtract the top-left or top-right 2x2 corner crop selected by the top edge clue.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The input is a square color grid whose answer is one of the two 2x2 crops\\\\n  touching the top edge and a grid corner.\\\\n- A repeated color on the top row, when present, acts as the primary side cue.\\\\n- Otherwise, the two top corner colors have different whole-grid frequencies.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- If a top-row color repeats, find the repeated top-row occurrence nearest to\\\\n  a left or right edge and take the 2x2 top-corner crop on that side.\\\\n- If the top row has no repeated color, compare the whole-grid frequencies of\\\\n  the two top-corner colors and take the side whose corner color is rarer.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The task is not asking for an arbitrary 2x2 search: the decisive information\\\\n  is on the top edge, and it selects which top corner crop to keep.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"2ba387bc\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"6-21\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\\\\n- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\\\\n- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\\\\n- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\\\\n- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\\\\n- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"1b59e163\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"54-69\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCopy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.\\\\n- Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Clear the grid to background.\\\\n- For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.\\\\n- Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"f0100645\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"51-68\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSlide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.\\\\n- One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.\\\\n- Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Clear the extra objects from their original positions.\\\\n- For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.\\\\n- Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.\\\\n- Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9f8de559\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"19-37\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nErase the first border pixel hit by extending the red marker away from its pink trail.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The dominant background surrounds a unique red marker and a four-pixel\\\\n  pink trail.\\\\n- The pink pixels form one straight 8-connected ray starting next to the\\\\n  red marker.\\\\n- In the opposite direction from that trail, the red marker faces a\\\\n  non-background border or obstacle pixel beyond background cells.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Keep the whole grid fixed except for the first non-background pixel on\\\\n  the ray from the red marker away from the pink trail.\\\\n- Recolor that one hit pixel to the background color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The pink trail marks where the red marker came from, so the edit is found\\\\n  by ray-casting from the red marker in the opposite direction.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"136b0064\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"25-39\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nDraw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.\\\\n- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.\\\\n- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).\\\\n- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.\\\\n- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"1478ab18\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"35-43\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPaint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.\\\\nRule\\\\nFind the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"45a5af55\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"5-18\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nBuild nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\\\n- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Read stripes bottom to top.\\\\n- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\\\\n- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"12\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"e87109e9\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"68-83\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nEmit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.\\\\n- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Remove the legend from the output.\\\\n- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).\\\\n- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.\\\\n- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.\\\\n- Beams stop at grid edges.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"13\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"5b37cb25\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"59-73\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFill each plus-shaped background notch with the color of the frame side it opens toward.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- A one-cell-thick rectangular frame has four solid-colored sides and neutral corner pixels.\\\\n- The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.\\\\n- Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.\\\\n- Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.\\\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe frame side colors are direction labels for the open notches in the foreground object.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"14\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9b30e358\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"9-23\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRepeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_053229_seed218530468_gpt54_high_resume/seed218530468__7__codegen_prompts__3.log:19:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/52364a65.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"from __future__ import annotations\\\\n\\\\nimport numpy as np\\\\n\\\\nfrom arc_utils import find_components, get_bg, paste, random_free_location, random_sprite\\\\nimport random\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\\\n    - Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\\\n    - Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\\\n    - Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight:\\\\n    - The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    bg = get_bg(g)\\\\n    components = find_components(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4, monochromatic=True)\\\\n    assert components, \\\\\\\"expected at least one foreground object\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n    out = g.copy()\\\\n    for component in components:\\\\n        coords = component[\\\\\\\"coords\\\\\\\"]\\\\n        _r0, c0, _r1, c1 = map(int, component[\\\\\\\"bbox\\\\\\\"])\\\\n        assert c1 - c0 + 1 >= 2, \\\\\\\"each object must span at least two columns\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n        erase = coords[coords[:, 1] < c0 + 2]\\\\n        out[erase[:, 0], erase[:, 1]] = bg\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (att1, Claude) ---------------\\\\n# Canvas constraints.\\\\nBG = 8\\\\nGRID_SIZE_RANGE = (8, 11)\\\\nMIN_BACKGROUND_FRACTION = 0.50\\\\n# Object sampling constraints.\\\\nOBJECT_COUNT = 4\\\\nFOREGROUND_COLORS = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9]\\\\nSPRITE_WIDTH_RANGE = (2, 6)\\\\nSPRITE_HEIGHT_RANGE = (2, 5)\\\\nSPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE = (4, 14)\\\\nSPRITE_RETRIES = 30\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 4\\\\nSPRITE_SYMMETRY = \\\\\\\"not_symmetric\\\\\\\"\\\\n# Placement and global retry policy.\\\\nPLACEMENT_PADDING = 1\\\\nPLACEMENT_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nGENERATION_RETRIES = 300\\\\n\\\\ndef _sample_sprite(color: int) -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return one connected sprite that lands inside the configured pixel-count range.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bw = random.randint(*SPRITE_WIDTH_RANGE)\\\\n    bh = random.randint(*SPRITE_HEIGHT_RANGE)\\\\n    max_px = bw * bh\\\\n    min_px = max(SPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE[0], bw + bh - 1)\\\\n    max_target_px = min(SPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE[1], max_px)\\\\n    if min_px > max_target_px:\\\\n        return None\\\\n    target_px = random.randint(min_px, max_target_px)\\\\n    density = target_px / max_px\\\\n    for _ in range(SPRITE_RETRIES):\\\\n        try:\\\\n            sprite = random_sprite(bh, bw, density=density, color_palette=[color],\\\\n                                   connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY, background=BG,\\\\n                                   symmetry=SPRITE_SYMMETRY)\\\\n        except Exception:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        px = int(np.sum(sprite != BG))\\\\n        if SPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE[0] <= px <= SPRITE_PIXEL_RANGE[1]:\\\\n            return sprite\\\\n    return None\\\\n\\\\ndef _place_sprite(grid: np.ndarray, sprite: np.ndarray) -> bool:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Paste sprite with the required Chebyshev gap; return False if no slot exists.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    try:\\\\n        r, c = random_free_location(grid, sprite, transparent=BG,\\\\n                                    padding=PLACEMENT_PADDING,\\\\n                                    padding_connectivity=PLACEMENT_CONNECTIVITY)\\\\n    except ValueError:\\\\n        return False\\\\n    paste(grid, sprite, r, c, transparent=BG)\\\\n    return True\\\\n\\\\ndef _solver_accepts(grid: np.ndarray) -> bool:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return whether the solver accepts the sampled task instance.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    try:\\\\n        out = main(grid)\\\\n    except Exception:\\\\n        return False\\\\n    return out is not None\\\\n\\\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\n    H = random.randint(*GRID_SIZE_RANGE)\\\\n    W = random.randint(*GRID_SIZE_RANGE)\\\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), BG, dtype=int)\\\\n    for color in random.sample(FOREGROUND_COLORS, OBJECT_COUNT):\\\\n        sprite = _sample_sprite(color)\\\\n        if sprite is None or not _place_sprite(grid, sprite):\\\\n            return None\\\\n    if np.sum(grid == BG) / grid.size < MIN_BACKGROUND_FRACTION:\\\\n        return None\\\\n    return grid if _solver_accepts(grid) else None\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_RETRIES):\\\\n        result = _gen_attempt()\\\\n        if result is not None:\\\\n            return result\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(f\\\\\\\"Failed to generate input after {GENERATION_RETRIES} attempts\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed385645705/15/7.py:102:    - The leftmost column contains a vertical legend of distinct colors whose top-to-bottom order defines growth priority.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__13__codegen_prompts__2.log:37:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_18\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '/\\\\\\\"'^def main(/,/''^def /p'\\\\\\\"' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py | sed '\\\\\\\"'$d'\\\\\\\"'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    H, W = g.shape\\\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__1__codegen_prompts__6.log:46:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_23\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/1/des.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内散落碎片的颜色，将该区域的边框重新着色为碎片颜色；同时将碎片本身替换为边框原来的颜色。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干由单一颜色线段围成的封闭矩形边框，每个边框的颜色各不相同。每个边框内部除了黑色背景外，还散落着若干像素碎片，这些碎片的颜色与该边框不同，但与网格中另一个边框的颜色相同。每种碎片颜色在所有边框内部只出现一次（即每个边框内只有一种非背景碎片颜色）。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个封闭矩形边框，找到其内部散落碎片的颜色 C_inner。将该边框的所有边框像素重新着色为 C_inner。同时，将边框内部的碎片像素替换为该边框原来的颜色 C_border。边框内部的背景像素保持黑色不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现边框内碎片颜色与其他边框颜色之间的\\\\\\\"颜色交换\\\\\\\"映射关系，然后理解变换是边框与内部碎片之间的颜色互换——碎片的颜色告诉你边框该变成什么色，而边框的原色则回填到碎片位置上。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：每个带箭头标记的色块沿箭头方向\\\\\\\"印章式\\\\\\\"复制自身，复制次数由该色块内部孔洞的数量决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不接触的单色连通色块（4-连通），每个色块是不规则形状，其中可能包含零个或多个由背景色形成的内部孔洞（被色块像素完全包围的黑色区域）。每个色块的外侧恰好有一个由 red 像素组成的箭头标记，箭头由三个像素构成：一个尖端像素和两个沿对角线分布的翼像素，整体指向上、下、左、右四个方向之一。箭头尖端与色块边缘恰好相邻（4-邻接）。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个色块，数出其内部孔洞的数量 N。沿箭头指向的方向，在色块的前方，以色块自身的外接矩形宽度（或高度，取决于方向）加 1 格间距为步长，连续复制 N 份该色块的完整形状（包括孔洞保持为黑色）。若 N=0，则色块保持原样不复制。箭头标记在输出中被擦除（变为背景色）。色块本身保留在原位。\\\\n- `Key insight`：箭头仅提供复制方向，而复制次数这一关键信息隐藏在色块自身的拓扑结构中——内部孔洞数即为复制份数。解题者需要同时识别方向线索（箭头）和数量线索（孔洞），并理解它们分别控制变换的不同维度。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：将网格中由分隔线划分的若干面板按照隐含的拼图逻辑重新排列，使得相邻面板的边缘花纹能够无缝对接。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格被 grey 色的单像素宽分隔线均匀划分为 m*n 个等大矩形面板（例如 2*3 或 3*3）。每个面板内部包含彩色图案，且每个面板的四条边缘（紧邻分隔线或网格边界的那一行/列像素）上有特定的颜色序列花纹。整个网格中恰好存在唯一一种排列方式，使得每对相邻面板的共享边缘花纹完全一致（即左面板的右边缘与右面板的左边缘像素逐一相同，上面板的下边缘与下面板的上边缘像素逐一相同）。输入中面板的排列是打乱的。\\\\n- `Rule`：找到所有面板的唯一正确排列，使得每对 4-邻接的面板共享边缘花纹完全匹配。将面板按正确顺序重新放入同样大小的网格中，保留 grey 分隔线。面板内容不做任何修改，仅改变其在网格中的位置。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要将每个面板的四条边缘花纹视为\\\\\\\"拼图接口\\\\\\\"，通过逐对匹配边缘花纹来推断正确的空间排列。关键在于识别出边缘花纹是匹配线索，而非面板内部图案——内部图案是干扰项，真正决定排列的是边缘处的颜色序列。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：识别网格中每个\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\"对象发射的十字射线，根据射线交叉点处的叠加规则确定交叉像素的最终颜色，再将每座塔按其实际覆盖的独占射线长度从长到短排序，输出为对应颜色的竖条。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个\\\\\\\"信号塔\\\\\\\"，每座塔是一个 3*3 的单色实心方块，颜色各不相同。从每座塔的中心像素出发，向上、下、左、右四个方向发射与塔同色的射线，射线延伸至网格边界。当两条不同颜色的射线在某个像素交叉时，该像素显示为较大面积塔（3*3 方块面积不算，只看射线覆盖的总像素数更多的那座塔）的颜色。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步：为每座塔画出从中心向四个方向延伸到网格边界的十字射线（不覆盖其他塔的 3*3 方块区域，射线遇到其他塔的方块时截断）。第二步：在射线交叉点处，比较两座塔各自的射线总长度（四个方向之和），用射线总长度较长的塔的颜色覆盖交叉像素。第三步：统计每座塔最终独占的射线像素数（被覆盖的不算），按独占数从大到小排序。第四步：输出一个 1*K 的网格（K 为塔的数量），每个像素按排序顺序填入对应塔的颜色。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题需要三层推理——先构建射线并理解交叉处的覆盖规则（射线总长决定优先级），再统计覆盖后的独占像素数，最后将排序结果编码为颜色条。表面上看到的是彩色十字交叉图案，但规则的核心是\\\\\\\"射线长度决定交叉优先级\\\\\\\"这一非显然的叠加逻辑。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：在由彩色路径连接的节点图中，每个节点根据与其相连的路径颜色混合规则变换自身颜色，路径本身则继承其两端节点变换后颜色的选择结果。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干个 2*2 的单色实心方块作为\\\\\\\"节点\\\\\\\"，节点颜色各不相同。节点之间通过单像素宽的彩色直线路径（水平或垂直）连接，每条路径有自己的颜色，且路径颜色与其两端节点的颜色都不同。每个节点恰好连接 2 条或 3 条路径。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步——节点变色：对于每个节点，收集与其相连的所有路径的颜色。如果恰好有 2 条路径，节点变为这两条路径中在 ARC 标准色序（Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon）中排位靠前的那个颜色。如果有 3 条路径，节点变为排位居中的那个颜色。第二步——路径变色：每条路径连接两个节点，取两端节点变换后的新颜色——如果两端新颜色相同，路径变为该颜色；如果不同，路径变为两者中色序排位靠后的那个。节点和路径的形状与位置保持不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题者需要先发现节点颜色的变换依赖于路径颜色的某种选择规则（需要从样例中归纳出\\\\\\\"色序排位\\\\\\\"这一隐含排序），然后发现路径的变换又反过来依赖于节点变换后的结果。两步变换形成依赖链——必须先完成所有节点变色，才能确定路径的新颜色，而色序排位规则本身需要从多个样例的对比中归纳得出。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：将每个彩色形状按其\\\\\\\"影子投影\\\\\\\"方向压扁为单像素宽的色条，投影方向由形状内部唯一的标记像素相对于形状重心的位置决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有若干互不接触的单色连通形状（4-连通），每个形状内部恰好嵌入一个 red 标记像素（该像素替换了形状原本颜色的一个像素）。形状各自颜色不同且均非 red 或黑色。每个形状的外接矩形不与其他形状重叠。\\\\n- `Rule`：对于每个形状，找到其外接矩形的几何中心（取外接矩形行范围和列范围的中点）。观察 red 标记像素相对于该中心的方位：若标记在中心的正上方或正下方（同列或偏差不超过1列），则投影方向为垂直方向——将形状沿垂直方向压缩，即统计形状在每一列上是否存在像素，输出为一个水平色条（单像素高），色条放置在形状外接矩形的垂直中心行，色条长度等于形状在水平方向的跨度，每个有像素存在的列着形状色，无像素的列保持黑色。若标记在中心的正左方或正右方（同行或偏差不超过1行），则投影方向为水平方向——将形状沿水平方向压缩，输出为一个竖直色条（单像素宽），放置在外接矩形的水平中心列。red 标记像素在输出中被擦除，原形状的其余像素也被擦除，仅保留投影后的色条。\\\\n- `Key insight`：red 标记看似只是一个位置标注，实则它与形状重心的相对方位编码了投影轴的选择。解题者需要先归纳出\\\\\\\"标记相对于重心的方向决定压缩轴\\\\\\\"这一规律，再理解\\\\\\\"压缩\\\\\\\"操作是将形状沿该轴做列（或行）存在性投影。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<new_puzzle>\\\\n- `description`：在被色框分隔的子区域中，每个区域内的散点图案需要被\\\\\\\"传送\\\\\\\"到由隐藏配对规则指定的另一个区域，配对规则由框的边长奇偶性决定。\\\\n- `Input structure`：背景为黑色。网格中有偶数个（如 4 个或 6 个）不重叠的单色空心矩形框，每个框的颜色各不相同。每个框内部（框线以内的区域）包含一组由某种非框色、非背景色的颜色绘制的散点图案（连通或不连通均可），不同框内的散点图案颜色也各不相同。\\\\n- `Rule`：第一步——框的配对：将所有框按照边长奇偶性分组。具体地，计算每个框的宽度（列数）和高度（行数）。将\\\\\\\"宽为奇、高为奇\\\\\\\"的框归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为偶、高为偶\\\\\\\"的框归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为奇、高为偶\\\\\\\"归为一组，\\\\\\\"宽为偶、高为奇\\\\\\\"归为一组。每组内恰好有两个框，它们构成一对。第二步——图案交换：对于配对的两个框 A 和 B，将 A 内部的散点图案（保持相对于 A 框左上角内侧的偏移不变）搬移到 B 的内部（以 B 框左上角内侧为锚点，相同偏移放置），同时将 B 的散点图案搬到 A 内。散点图案保持原来的颜色不变。框本身保持不变。\\\\n- `Key insight`：框的配对规则隐藏在框的几何属性中——宽高的奇偶组合将框两两配对。解题者需要先发现\\\\\\\"哪个框的内容去了哪里\\\\\\\"（观察图案的形状在不同框间的交换），再从框的尺寸中归纳出配对依据是宽高奇偶性的组合匹配，最后理解图案是以锚点对齐方式搬移的。\\\\n</new_puzzle>\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__1__codegen_prompts__6.log:74:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_40\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"agent_message\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"已将实现写入 [6.py](/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1852178230/1/6.py)。`main()` 按连通形状识别、bbox 中心与 red 标记相对方位判定投影轴，并把每个对象压成中心水平/竖直色条；`generate_input()` 会随机生成不同尺寸、数量、颜色、位置和两种方向分支的样例，并保证对象 bbox 分离且可唯一判定。\\\\n\\\\n已按要求完成自检：100 次随机样例检查通过，`variants 100`；`python -m py_compile` 通过；验证产生的 `__pycache__` 已清理。\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/7/codegen_prompts/4.md:12:- `description`：将每个多色精灵中的颜色分量分离，每种颜色在精灵的位置生成一个独立的投影副本，投影方向由颜色在精灵中的位置决定。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/7/codegen_prompts/4.md:19:- `Key insight`：标记色像素是方向编码器——其在精灵中的相对位置决定了投影轮廓的方向；解题者需要发现这种\\\"位置→方向\\\"的映射，而非将标记色视为要着色或移动的对象。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:307:Erase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/13_1.log:315:- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/5/5.py:112:    - Identify whether the rectangle has horizontal stripes (each row is constant) or vertical stripes (each column is constant).\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/5/5.py:114:    - Roll horizontal stripes vertically by D cells, or roll vertical stripes horizontally by D cells, preserving the rectangle shape.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__7__codegen_prompts__6.log:45:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_22\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"rg -n '' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/7/prompt.md | sed -n '1,220p'\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n2:\\\\n3:每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n8:\\\\n9:参考题目如下：\\\\n10:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"7666fa5d\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"12-26\\\\\\\">\\\\n11:<description>\\\\n12:Fill the parallelogram-shaped region between parallel anti-diagonal line segments with red.\\\\n13:\\\\n14:Input structure:\\\\n15:- bg = most common color.\\\\n16:- One non-bg color forms short diagonal segments, each lying on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = const).\\\\n17:- Segments come in parallel pairs bounding a region to be filled.\\\\n18:\\\\n19:Rule:\\\\n20:- For each main-diagonal axis (r−c = const), collect anti-diagonal segments whose span covers that axis.\\\\n21:- Sort those segments by their anti-diagonal index (r+c).\\\\n22:- Fill all bg cells lying strictly between consecutive segment pairs along that axis with red (color 2).\\\\n23:\\\\n24:Key insight: The two diagonal directions decouple — segments sit on anti-diagonals, and filling sweeps along main diagonals between them, forming parallelogram regions.\\\\n25:</description>\\\\n26:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n27:\\\\n28:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"da515329\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"11-24\\\\\\\">\\\\n29:<description>\\\\n30:Grow four clockwise spiral wall paths from the tips of a teal cross.\\\\n31:\\\\n32:Input structure:\\\\n33:- bg = 0 (black). A single teal (8) cross centered in the grid.\\\\n34:\\\\n35:Rule:\\\\n36:- Each arm tip launches a \\\\\\\"turtle\\\\\\\" heading 90° right of its outward direction.\\\\n37:- Movement priority: turn right > go straight > turn left (left only if not on border).\\\\n38:- Normal step = 2 cells; step right after a turn = 1 cell.\\\\n39:- Each new cell must have a 1-cell orthogonal gap from all existing walls except the predecessor.\\\\n40:\\\\n41:Key insight: The right-turn preference plus alternating 2/1 step lengths creates self-avoiding spirals that tile the grid with uniform spacing.\\\\n42:</description>\\\\n43:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n44:\\\\n45:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"fbf15a0b\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"49-69\\\\\\\">\\\\n46:<description>\\\\n47:Crop out the grid half containing the two aligned marker pixels, then erase the markers to background.\\\\n48:\\\\n49:Input structure\\\\n50:- The grid has a dominant background color and one non-background marker color\\\\n51:  that appears as exactly two cells.\\\\n52:- The marker cells are aligned either in one row or one column and both lie\\\\n53:  in the same half along that direction.\\\\n54:- Other non-background pixels are content inside one or both halves.\\\\n55:\\\\n56:Rule\\\\n57:- If the markers share a row, keep the left or right half whose columns\\\\n58:  contain them.\\\\n59:- If the markers share a column, keep the top or bottom half whose rows\\\\n60:  contain them.\\\\n61:- In the kept half, recolor the marker pixels to the background color.\\\\n62:\\\\n63:Key insight\\\\n64:- The two marker pixels are not part of the picture; their alignment and\\\\n65:  half-position identify which half of the doubled canvas is the answer.\\\\n66:</description>\\\\n67:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n68:\\\\n69:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"b71a7747\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"10-23\\\\\\\">\\\\n70:<description>\\\\n71:Extract the hidden two-color image by compacting the rows and columns of its complete mask.\\\\n72:\\\\n73:Input structure\\\\n74:The grid contains one pair of colors whose pixels occupy every cell in the\\\\n75:cross product of their active rows and active columns; all other colors form\\\\n76:the surrounding filler or separators.\\\\n77:Rule\\\\n78:Find that unique color pair, keep exactly the rows and columns touched by\\\\n79:the pair, and return the induced subgrid.\\\\n80:Key insight\\\\n81:The target image is not chosen by color id; it is the only two-color mask\\\\n82:whose occupied pixels form a full rectangular row/column product after\\\\n83:deleting unused rows and columns.\\\\n84:</description>\\\\n85:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n86:\\\\n87:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"15660dd6\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"33-54\\\\\\\">\\\\n88:<description>\\\\n89:Combine each column's repeated template mask with its single solid color swatch.\\\\n90:\\\\n91:Input structure:\\\\n92:- The grid is a table of framed panels separated by background rows/columns.\\\\n93:- The leftmost column gives one solid row-label color for each panel row.\\\\n94:- In each panel column, exactly one panel has a solid non-background interior,\\\\n95:  while the other panels share the same mask drawn in one template color on\\\\n96:  the background.\\\\n97:\\\\n98:Rule:\\\\n99:- For every panel column, find the row containing the solid interior swatch.\\\\n100:- Rebuild one output panel using that row's left label as the frame color.\\\\n101:- Fill the repeated template mask with the swatch color and leave the mask\\\\n102:  background cells as background; separate rebuilt panels with one\\\\n103:  background column.\\\\n104:\\\\n105:Key insight:\\\\n106:The table encodes a colorized stencil per column: the solid panel supplies\\\\n107:the paint color and frame label, while the duplicate template panels supply\\\\n108:the shape mask.\\\\n109:</description>\\\\n110:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n111:\\\\n112:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"fc4aaf52\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"17-34\\\\\\\">\\\\n113:<description>\\\\n114:Split the two-color object horizontally, swap its colors, and slide the upper half to the right.\\\\n115:\\\\n116:Input structure:\\\\n117:- The grid has one background color and exactly two foreground colors.\\\\n118:- All foreground pixels form one 4-connected object with an even-height bbox.\\\\n119:- The object has foreground pixels on both rows adjacent to its horizontal midpoint.\\\\n120:\\\\n121:Rule:\\\\n122:- Split the object into upper and lower halves at the midpoint of its bbox.\\\\n123:- Swap the two foreground colors in both halves.\\\\n124:- Keep the lower half in place and shift the upper half right until its lower-left\\\\n125:  boundary pixel is diagonally adjacent to the lower half's upper-right boundary pixel.\\\\n126:\\\\n127:Key insight:\\\\n128:- The object is not copied or reflected; it is broken at the horizontal waist,\\\\n129:  recolored by exchanging the two visible object colors, then rejoined diagonally.\\\\n130:</description>\\\\n131:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n132:\\\\n133:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"68bc2e87\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"46-60\\\\\\\">\\\\n134:<description>\\\\n135:Recover the bottom-to-top stacking order of overlaid rectangular color frames.\\\\n136:\\\\n137:Input structure:\\\\n138:- The background is one color, and every foreground color is a one-cell-thick rectangular frame.\\\\n139:- Overlapping frame pixels show only the color of the frame that is highest at that location.\\\\n140:\\\\n141:Rule:\\\\n142:- Reconstruct each frame as the border of the bounding box of its visible pixels.\\\\n143:- At every cell covered by multiple reconstructed frames, the visible frame color is above the other frames covering that cell.\\\\n144:- Return the unique bottom-to-top order of frame colors as a single-column grid.\\\\n145:\\\\n146:Key insight:\\\\n147:The hidden parts of each frame do not need to be seen directly; the visible pixels reveal the full frame bbox, and overlap cells reveal the layer constraints.\\\\n148:</description>\\\\n149:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n150:\\\\n151:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"7d7772cc\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"70-92\\\\\\\">\\\\n152:<description>\\\\n153:Move each source pixel toward the separator when it matches its aligned reference pixel, otherwise to the far edge.\\\\n154:\\\\n155:Input structure:\\\\n156:- A single full separator line is part of a rectangular frame; the frame's\\\\n157:  extra cells mark the reference side.\\\\n158:- On the reference side, one row or column of colored pixels is aligned\\\\n159:  with one row or column of source pixels on the opposite side.\\\\n160:- Each side has its own dominant background color.\\\\n161:\\\\n162:Rule:\\\\n163:- Compare each source pixel with the reference pixel on the same row or column.\\\\n164:- If their colors match, place the source pixel in the cell adjacent to the\\\\n165:  separator on the source side.\\\\n166:- If their colors differ, place the source pixel on the far outer edge along\\\\n167:  the same row or column.\\\\n168:- Erase the original source pixels to the source-side background; keep the\\\\n169:  frame and reference pixels unchanged.\\\\n170:\\\\n171:Key insight:\\\\n172:The extra frame cells identify which side is the reference; equality with the\\\\n173:aligned reference pixel decides whether each source pixel moves inward or outward.\\\\n174:</description>\\\\n175:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n176:\\\\n177:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"48634b99\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"14-27\\\\\\\">\\\\n178:<description>\\\\n179:Advance the marker from one half of a vertical bar to the same half of the next longer bar.\\\\n180:\\\\n181:Input structure\\\\n182:- The grid has one dominant background color and exactly two foreground colors.\\\\n183:- One foreground color forms many vertical one-cell-wide bars; the other appears as a single vertical marker segment.\\\\n184:- The marker segment occupies exactly the top or bottom half of its containing vertical bar.\\\\n185:Rule\\\\n186:- Recolor the current marker segment back to the bar color.\\\\n187:- Find the unique all-bar-color vertical bar whose height is two pixels greater than the marked source bar.\\\\n188:- Recolor the same half of that next longer bar to the marker color.\\\\n189:Key insight\\\\n190:- Each bar's total height encodes an ordered size, and the marker advances from a 2k bar to the corresponding 2(k+1) bar while preserving whether it marks the top or bottom half.\\\\n191:</description>\\\\n192:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n193:\\\\n194:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"a416fc5b\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"95-106\\\\\\\">\\\\n195:<description>\\\\n196:Add the two missing colored arms of a centered diamond-sprite motif, or clear a completed motif to a blank square.\\\\n197:\\\\n198:Input structure\\\\n199:An 11x11 board has orange background and pink separator bars forming nine 3x3 cells. Occupied cells contain a four-pixel diamond sprite; the center cell and one neighboring cell are red, and a completed board may also contain one grey and one teal sprite.\\\\n200:\\\\n201:Rule\\\\n202:With only the two red sprites present, preserve the board and add grey and teal diamond sprites 135 degrees clockwise and counterclockwise from the non-center red arm. If those expected grey and teal sprites are already present, output an all-background square whose side length is the total number of sprite pixels.\\\\n203:\\\\n204:Key insight\\\\n205:The non-center red sprite is an eight-neighbor direction from the center; the other two colored arms are fixed rotations of that direction.\\\\n206:</description>\\\\n207:</reference_puzzle>\\\\n208:\\\\n209:<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"a47bf94d\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"178-189\\\\\\\">\\\\n210:<description>\\\\n211:Transmit colored tokens along wire networks, converting each to its complementary 3×3 pattern.\\\\n212:\\\\n213:Input structure:\\\\n214:- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.\\\\n215:\\\\n216:Rule:\\\\n217:- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).\\\\n218:- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.\\\\n219:\\\\n220:Key insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260617_223106_seed2047415201/1__3.py.log:32:  - 在每组内，按箭头在朝向方向上的投影坐标从近到远排序。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260617_223106_seed2047415201/1__3.py.log:16232:我现在准备写入目标实现。核心做法是按同色 4 连通组件识别 2x2 三像素箭头，用缺失角定方向，用相对对应角落的投影排序，然后把每组颜色写成从对应角落向内的单像素对角线。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__13__codegen_prompts__6.log:50:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_25\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/13/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"bae5c565\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"10-28\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nErase the top palette row and redraw it below as a widening wedge centered on its missing cell.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The top row is a palette row with exactly one background gap.\\\\n- Below it, the only foreground is one vertical marker bar of a single color.\\\\n- The marker bar is either in the gap column or immediately beside it.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Clear the grid to background.\\\\n- Starting at the top of the marker bar, each next row copies one more\\\\n  column of the top-row palette on both sides of the gap.\\\\n- Fill the gap column with the marker color, and keep the vertical marker bar.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The lone background cell in the top row is the center of the expanding\\\\n  copy; the lower vertical bar provides the center color and the row where\\\\n  the expansion begins.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"470c91de\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"48-65\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each teal-cornered filled rectangle one cell diagonally toward its teal corner.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Dominant background surrounds several filled rectangular colored objects.\\\\n- Each object has exactly one teal control pixel replacing one corner cell of\\\\n  its rectangle.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Treat the teal pixel as the missing corner of its colored rectangle.\\\\n- Erase each original rectangle footprint, including the teal pixel.\\\\n- Repaint the completed rectangle shifted one cell diagonally in the direction\\\\n  of that teal corner.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The control pixel's corner position gives both the missing cell to restore\\\\n  and the diagonal motion vector.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"3d6c6e23\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"10-27\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nMove each vertical stream of pixels into a bottom-aligned centered pile.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- A mostly background grid contains one or more vertical source columns of\\\\n  foreground pixels.\\\\n- Each source column has n^2 foreground pixels, and the top-to-bottom color\\\\n  sequence splits into monochrome groups of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Clear the canvas to background.\\\\n- For each source column, read the foreground colors from top to bottom and\\\\n  rebuild them at the bottom below the same column as odd-width centered\\\\n  rows of lengths 1, 3, 5, ...\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The scattered vertical pixels are falling grains; a square number of\\\\n  grains decomposes into the odd row widths of a centered pyramid.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"13f06aa5\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"36-51\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExtend each colored marker from its directional sprite to a grid edge, painting a dotted ray and the whole edge side.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- One repeated body color forms small 8-connected directional sprites.\\\\n- Each marker is a singleton non-background, non-body color embedded in one sprite.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- The body pixels around a marker lie mostly behind it; the opposite direction is the marker's ray direction.\\\\n- Paint every second pixel from the marker along that ray, then paint the entire boundary side reached by the ray.\\\\n- If two painted boundary sides meet at a corner, make that shared corner black.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The same seven-pixel body sprite rotates to encode the direction; its local center-of-mass bias points away from the ray.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"2c181942\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"7-21\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = background. A hollow NxN square (hub) with bg corners/interior and four differently-colored edges (top, bottom, left, right).\\\\n- 2-4 monochrome sprites scattered on the grid, each matching one hub edge color.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- For each hub edge color, find the matching sprite outside the hub.\\\\n- Rotate the sprite (0/90/180/270°) so its contact edge has exactly N-2 contiguous cells aligned with the hub side, and the rotated sprite is mirror-symmetric along the contact-edge axis (UD for left/right, LR for top/bottom).\\\\n- Translate it to adjoin that hub side. \\\\n- Clear everything else to bg; output is hub + attached sprites only.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Each edge color uniquely pairs a sprite to a side; symmetry along the contact-edge axis disambiguates the correct rotation.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"79cce52d\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"29-44\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCrop off the control row and column, then cyclically roll the payload by the two marker offsets.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The grid is square, with a control row on top and a control column on the left.\\\\n- The control row and column share one filler color and one single-pixel marker color.\\\\n- The lower-right square is the payload and contains none of the control colors.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Remove the top control row and left control column.\\\\n- Roll the remaining payload down by the marker's zero-based position in the left control column.\\\\n- Roll the payload right by the marker's zero-based position in the top control row.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The two border markers are cyclic shift amounts for the payload, not colors to preserve.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"30f42897\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"51-66\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRepeat the single colored border segment around the rectangular border, leaving one segment-length gap between copies.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- There is exactly one foreground color.\\\\n- All foreground pixels form one contiguous segment on the rectangular border, possibly crossing the cycle start.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Unwrap the grid border clockwise into a cyclic path.\\\\n- Let n be the length of the foreground segment.\\\\n- Copy the segment with the same color every 2*n border positions around the cycle.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The foreground segment is not extended by rows or columns directly; it is a motif on the perimeter cycle, repeated with an equal-sized gap.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"52364a65\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"10-24\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nErase the two leftmost columns of every foreground object, leaving the rest of each object in place.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- A grid has one dominant background color and several monochromatic 4-connected foreground objects.\\\\n- Each foreground object spans at least two columns in its bounding box.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Find each same-color 4-connected foreground object.\\\\n- Within each object's own bounding box, set foreground pixels in the two leftmost columns to the background color.\\\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- The deletion is measured from each object's local left edge, not from the grid edge or from a shared global column.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"ad38a9d0\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"23-36\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRecolor each placeholder object according to its normalized shape while leaving the background fixed.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nA same-size grid with one dominant background color and one foreground\\\\nplaceholder color forming separated 4-connected objects.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nReplace every placeholder object by the color assigned to its exact\\\\ntranslation-normalized mask; all background pixels remain unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe input objects are a shape legend with repeated instances: identical\\\\nmasks always receive identical colors, independent of their position.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"5034a0b5\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"16-32\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nShift each interior pixel whose color matches a frame side one cell toward that matching side.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe grid has a one-cell-thick rectangular frame: the four corners are the\\\\nbackground color, and each side between corners is a solid, distinct side\\\\ncolor. The interior is mostly background with sparse foreground pixels.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nInterior pixels with the top-side color move one row up, bottom-side color\\\\nmove one row down, left-side color move one column left, and right-side color\\\\nmove one column right. A pixel already adjacent to its matching side stays in\\\\nplace; colors that do not match a frame side and the frame itself are unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe colored frame sides act as direction labels for matching interior pixels.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"42f83767\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"23-39\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExpand the lower color grid by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\\\\nThe legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\\\\nthe same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nPair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\\\\nthe lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\\\\nrecoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/17/codegen_prompts/4.md:355:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/17/codegen_prompts/4.md:368:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/13/codegen_prompts/1.md:45:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/13/codegen_prompts/1.md:58:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_210747_seed1852178230_gpt54_high/seed1852178230__12__codegen_prompts__3.log:29:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_14\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1852178230/12/prompt.md\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\\\\n\\\\n每个参考题描述包含：\\\\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\\\\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\\\\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\\\\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\\\\n\\\\n参考题目如下：\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"1\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"409aa875\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"68-81\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFire projectiles from 3-pixel triangle sprites; mark collisions with maroon or blue.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color. Non-bg 3-pixel sprites shaped as axis-aligned L's or diagonal V's.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Each triangle has an apex and an emission direction determined by its shape: L-shapes fire diagonally away from the missing corner; V-shapes fire along the axis away from the open side.\\\\n- A projectile lands exactly 5 cells from the apex in the emission direction.\\\\n- If it hits an existing sprite, that entire sprite is recolored to maroon (9).\\\\n- If two projectiles land on the same empty cell, that cell becomes blue (1); a lone projectile on empty bg paints maroon (9).\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The triangle's orientation encodes both direction and target; dual-projectile collisions on open bg produce blue, not maroon.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"2\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"8f3a5a89\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"22-36\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPaint an inner border around the region reachable from a corner marker pixel.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color; wall color (blue) forms barriers dividing the grid.\\\\n- A unique single pixel (magenta) sits on one corner — the start marker.\\\\n- Some wall-colored pixels are structural (border-touching, enclosing regions); others are decorations.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Flood-fill from the marker corner to find all reachable bg cells, blocked by structural walls.\\\\n- Erase wall-colored decorations hidden behind structural walls (not reachable from marker side).\\\\n- Paint orange (color 7) on every reachable bg cell adjacent to a wall or grid edge — forming a 1-cell inner border.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Only border-connected wall components act as real barriers; interior wall fragments are decorations to be removed.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"3\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"4df5b0ae\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"27-41\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPack the colored sprites along the bottom edge from smallest to largest.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several monochrome 4-connected\\\\nforeground sprites; a full-grid one-cell frame may surround the scene.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\nRemove any full-grid rectangular frame, sort the remaining sprites by pixel\\\\narea from smallest to largest, and paste their bounding-box sprites left to\\\\nright with each sprite bottom-aligned.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe original locations do not determine the final slots; each sprite's area\\\\ngives the packing order, while its shape and color are preserved.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"4\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"a6953f00\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"45-63\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nExtract the top-left or top-right 2x2 corner crop selected by the top edge clue.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The input is a square color grid whose answer is one of the two 2x2 crops\\\\n  touching the top edge and a grid corner.\\\\n- A repeated color on the top row, when present, acts as the primary side cue.\\\\n- Otherwise, the two top corner colors have different whole-grid frequencies.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- If a top-row color repeats, find the repeated top-row occurrence nearest to\\\\n  a left or right edge and take the 2x2 top-corner crop on that side.\\\\n- If the top row has no repeated color, compare the whole-grid frequencies of\\\\n  the two top-corner colors and take the side whose corner color is rarer.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The task is not asking for an arbitrary 2x2 search: the decisive information\\\\n  is on the top edge, and it selects which top corner crop to keep.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"5\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"2ba387bc\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"6-21\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\\\\n- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\\\\n- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\\\\n- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\\\\n- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\\\\n- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"6\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"1b59e163\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"54-69\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nCopy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.\\\\n- Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Clear the grid to background.\\\\n- For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.\\\\n- Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight:\\\\n- A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"7\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"f0100645\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"51-68\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nSlide each inner colored object horizontally into the same-colored vertical wall until it touches an obstacle.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- The only foreground colors are two non-background colors.\\\\n- One foreground color fills the left column and the other fills the right column.\\\\n- Extra 8-connected objects of each wall color appear away from that color's wall.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Clear the extra objects from their original positions.\\\\n- For each wall color, process its 8-connected extra objects from nearest to farthest from the matching wall.\\\\n- Slide each object horizontally toward its matching wall as far as possible without overlapping the wall or an already settled object of the same color.\\\\n- Keep the two vertical wall columns fixed.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The side columns act like color-specific gravity walls: same-colored objects compact sideways against their own wall while preserving each object's shape.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"8\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9f8de559\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"19-37\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nErase the first border pixel hit by extending the red marker away from its pink trail.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The dominant background surrounds a unique red marker and a four-pixel\\\\n  pink trail.\\\\n- The pink pixels form one straight 8-connected ray starting next to the\\\\n  red marker.\\\\n- In the opposite direction from that trail, the red marker faces a\\\\n  non-background border or obstacle pixel beyond background cells.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Keep the whole grid fixed except for the first non-background pixel on\\\\n  the ray from the red marker away from the pink trail.\\\\n- Recolor that one hit pixel to the background color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\n- The pink trail marks where the red marker came from, so the edit is found\\\\n  by ray-casting from the red marker in the opposite direction.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"9\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"136b0064\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"25-39\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nDraw a polyline by decoding 3x3 glyph instructions read across a divided grid.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Left of a full-height vertical divider: 3x3 colored glyphs on bg.\\\\n- Right of divider: a single gray (5) start pixel.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Remove the divider; shift the gray start into the left canvas.\\\\n- Read glyphs in column-major order (left→right, top→bottom).\\\\n- Each glyph's shape (pixel area) encodes a segment: area 4 → down 2, area 5 → right 3, area 6 → left 4, area 7 → left 2.\\\\n- Append segments sequentially, stepping down one cell between each.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Glyph pixel count (area) uniquely determines both segment length and direction — the shape itself is the instruction.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"10\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"1478ab18\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"35-43\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nPaint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\nThe grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.\\\\nRule\\\\nFind the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"11\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"45a5af55\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"5-18\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nBuild nested square frames from a stack of horizontal color stripes.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\\\n- Each stripe has uniform color and variable height (1-4 rows).\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Read stripes bottom to top.\\\\n- Bottom stripe becomes the center solid square with side length = stripe height.\\\\n- Each subsequent stripe wraps the current shape with a square frame of thickness = stripe height, in that stripe's color.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: Stripe height doubles as both frame thickness and (for the innermost) center-square side length; output dimensions are fully determined by the stripe heights.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"12\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"eval\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"e87109e9\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"68-83\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nEmit four teal beams from a square, turning at colored obstacles per a legend.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure:\\\\n- Top band: grey (5) legend with colored vertical bars in cells; bar position (left or right) encodes turn direction.\\\\n- Below: main grid with bg, a solid teal (8) square, and colored obstacle blocks.\\\\n\\\\nRule:\\\\n- Remove the legend from the output.\\\\n- From the teal square, shoot a beam in each cardinal direction (as a sliding copy of the square).\\\\n- Each beam paints teal over bg cells as it moves.\\\\n- On hitting an obstacle of color C, consult the legend: bar on left → turn counterclockwise, bar on right → turn clockwise. Continue in the new direction.\\\\n- Beams stop at grid edges.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight: The legend's bar position (left vs right within its cell) is the encoding for turn direction at each obstacle color.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"13\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"5b37cb25\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"59-73\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nFill each plus-shaped background notch with the color of the frame side it opens toward.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- A one-cell-thick rectangular frame has four solid-colored sides and neutral corner pixels.\\\\n- The frame interior contains a dominant background color and one foreground object color.\\\\n- Some object boundaries contain five-pixel plus-shaped background notches.\\\\n\\\\nRule\\\\n- Find every background plus whose opposite side is supported by foreground object pixels and whose open side faces one frame side.\\\\n- Recolor the five pixels of that plus with the color of the facing frame side.\\\\n- Leave all other pixels unchanged.\\\\n\\\\nKey insight\\\\nThe frame side colors are direction labels for the open notches in the foreground object.\\\\n</description>\\\\n</reference_puzzle>\\\\n\\\\n<reference_puzzle index=\\\\\\\"14\\\\\\\" source=\\\\\\\"train\\\\\\\" puzzle_id=\\\\\\\"9b30e358\\\\\\\" lines=\\\\\\\"9-23\\\\\\\">\\\\n<description>\\\\nRepeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\\\\n\\\\nInput structure\\\\n- The background is the dominant color.\\\\n- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001243/5_4.log:2432:/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/2/3.py:142:    - A horizontal segment means fill the room with horizontal stripes; a vertical segment means fill it with vertical stripes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed241687935/_codegen_logs/run_20260619_001243/5_4.log:2616:    - A horizontal segment means fill the room with horizontal stripes; a vertical segment means fill it with vertical stripes.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/7_7.log:2919:  - 第三步：沿投射方向，从对象最外侧边缘的下一个像素开始，将对象在该方向上的投影轮廓（即沿投射方向看到的剪影）以 grey 颜色绘制 N 行（或 N 列），形成长度为 N 的影子。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/_codegen_logs/run_20260618_111948_seed807260302/seed807260302__3__codegen_prompts__4.log:23:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/bash -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '8,360p' /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/58490d8a.py\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.\\\\n\\\\n    Input structure:\\\\n    - A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.\\\\n    - Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.\\\\n\\\\n    Rule:\\\\n    - For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.\\\\n    - Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\\\\n\\\\n    Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\\\\n    H, W = g.shape\\\\n    _bg = int(get_bg(g))\\\\n\\\\n    black = 0\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\\\\n    best = None  # (area, bbox)\\\\n    for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\\\\n        if coords.size == 0:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        b = bbox_coords(coords)\\\\n        sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\\\\n        if (sub != int(black)).any():\\\\n            area = int(coords.shape[0])\\\\n            cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\\\\n            if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\\\\n                best = cand\\\\n\\\\n    assert not (best is None)\\\\n\\\\n    r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\\\\n    box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\\\\n    # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \\\\\\\"key pixels\\\\\\\").\\\\n    key_col = None\\\\n    for cc in range(bw):\\\\n        if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\\\\n            key_col = int(cc)\\\\n            break\\\\n    if key_col is None:\\\\n        return np.zeros_like(box)\\\\n\\\\n    keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\\\\n    keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\\\\n\\\\n    outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\\\\n    outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\\\\n    out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\\\\n\\\\n    # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\\\\n    for rr, col in keys:\\\\n        mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\\\\n        _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\\\\n        for i in range(int(nc)):\\\\n            cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\\\\n            if 0 <= cc < bw:\\\\n                out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\\\\n\\\\n    return out\\\\n\\\\n# --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\\\\n\\\\n# Palette and legend color choices.\\\\nCOLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\\\\nBLACK = 0\\\\nDISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\\\\n\\\\n# Key rows and tally dimensions.\\\\nKEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\\\\nTARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\\\\nKEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\\\\nKEY_ROW_STEP = 2\\\\nKEY_COLUMN = 1\\\\nTALLY_COL_STEP = 2\\\\nLEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\\\\nLEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\\\\n\\\\n# Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\\\\nGRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nGRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\\\\nLEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\\\\n\\\\n# Sprite shape and placement constraints.\\\\nSPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\\\\nSPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\\\\nSPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING = 1\\\\nSPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\\\\n\\\\n# Retry budget for rejection sampling.\\\\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _randint(bounds: tuple[int, int]) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return an inclusive randint from a configured (low, high) pair.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return random.randint(bounds[0], bounds[1])\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n@lru_cache(maxsize=None)\\\\ndef _valid_masks(h: int, w: int, area: int) -> tuple[np.ndarray, ...]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return connected masks that span all four sides of the sprite bbox.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    masks = []\\\\n    for cells in combinations(range(h * w), area):\\\\n        mask = np.zeros((h, w), dtype=bool)\\\\n        for cell in cells:\\\\n            mask[cell // w, cell % w] = True\\\\n        spans_edges = mask[0, :].any() and mask[-1, :].any() and mask[:, 0].any() and mask[:, -1].any()\\\\n        if not spans_edges:\\\\n            continue\\\\n        _, n = label_mask(mask, connectivity=SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY)\\\\n        if n == 1:\\\\n            masks.append(mask)\\\\n    return tuple(masks)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _make_sprite(color: int, bg: int) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample one connected same-color sprite drawn on the background color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    area = _randint(SPRITE_AREA_RANGE)\\\\n    dims = []\\\\n    for h, w in SPRITE_BBOXES:\\\\n        if h * w >= area and _valid_masks(h, w, area):\\\\n            dims.append((h, w))\\\\n    h, w = random.choice(dims)\\\\n    mask = random.choice(_valid_masks(h, w, area))\\\\n    sprite = np.full((h, w), int(bg), dtype=int)\\\\n    sprite[mask] = int(color)\\\\n    return sprite\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _sample_palette() -> tuple[int, list[int], int | None]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Choose background, key colors, and optional distractor color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    colors = list(COLOR_POOL)\\\\n    bg = random.choice(colors)\\\\n\\\\n    k = _randint(KEY_COUNT_RANGE)\\\\n    remaining = [c for c in colors if c != bg]\\\\n    key_colors = random.sample(remaining, k)\\\\n    remaining = [c for c in remaining if c not in key_colors]\\\\n    distractor_color = random.choice(remaining) if remaining and random.random() < DISTRACTOR_PROB else None\\\\n    return bg, key_colors, distractor_color\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _sample_counts(k: int) -> list[int]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample the target outside-component count for each key color.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return [_randint(TARGET_COUNT_RANGE) for _ in range(k)]\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _legend_shape(k: int, max_count: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return legend height and width for the key count and largest tally.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bh = KEY_ROW_STEP * k + LEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL\\\\n    bw = TALLY_COL_STEP * max_count + LEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL + _randint(LEGEND_SLACK_RANGE)\\\\n    return bh, bw\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _key_row(i: int) -> int:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Map a zero-based key index to its row inside the legend/output box.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    return KEY_ROW_FIRST + KEY_ROW_STEP * i\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_expected(key_colors: list[int], counts: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Render the black output tally canvas implied by key colors and counts.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    max_count = max(counts)\\\\n    bh, bw = _legend_shape(len(key_colors), max_count)\\\\n\\\\n    expected = np.full((bh, bw), BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\n    for i, (color, count) in enumerate(zip(key_colors, counts)):\\\\n        rr = _key_row(i)\\\\n        for j in range(count):\\\\n            expected[rr, KEY_COLUMN + TALLY_COL_STEP * j] = int(color)\\\\n    return expected\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_legend(shape: tuple[int, int], key_colors: list[int]) -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Return a black legend patch with only the key-column pixels filled.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    legend = np.full(shape, BLACK, dtype=int)\\\\n    for i, color in enumerate(key_colors):\\\\n        legend[_key_row(i), KEY_COLUMN] = int(color)\\\\n    return legend\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _new_grid_with_legend(bg: int, legend: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Sample a grid and paste the legend away from all canvas edges.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bh, bw = map(int, legend.shape)\\\\n    H = _randint(GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE)\\\\n    W = _randint(GRID_WIDTH_RANGE)\\\\n    min_h = bh + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\\\n    min_w = bw + 2 * LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN\\\\n    if H < min_h or W < min_w:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    grid = np.full((H, W), int(bg), dtype=int)\\\\n    r0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, H - bh - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\\\n    c0 = random.randint(LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN, W - bw - LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN)\\\\n    paste(grid, legend, r0, c0)\\\\n    return grid\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _build_sprite_queue(\\\\n    key_colors: list[int],\\\\n    counts: list[int],\\\\n    distractor_color: int | None,\\\\n    bg: int,\\\\n) -> list[np.ndarray]:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Create canonical key sprites, optional distractor sprite, and shuffle them.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    sprites = []\\\\n    for color, count in zip(key_colors, counts):\\\\n        sprite = _make_sprite(color, bg)\\\\n        for _ in range(count):\\\\n            sprites.append(sprite.copy())\\\\n    if distractor_color is not None:\\\\n        sprites.append(_make_sprite(distractor_color, bg))\\\\n    random.shuffle(sprites)\\\\n    return sprites\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _place_sprites(grid: np.ndarray, sprites: list[np.ndarray], bg: int) -> None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Paste sprites into random non-touching free locations in queue order.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    for sprite in sprites:\\\\n        sr, sc = random_free_location(\\\\n            grid,\\\\n            sprite,\\\\n            transparent=bg,\\\\n            padding=SPRITE_PADDING,\\\\n            padding_connectivity=SPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY,\\\\n        )\\\\n        paste(grid, sprite, sr, sc, transparent=bg)\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef _gen_attempt() -> np.ndarray | None:\\\\n    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Run one output-first generation attempt and reject solver mismatches.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bg, key_colors, distractor_color = _sample_palette()\\\\n    counts = _sample_counts(len(key_colors))\\\\n    expected = _build_expected(key_colors, counts)\\\\n    legend = _build_legend(expected.shape, key_colors)\\\\n    grid = _new_grid_with_legend(bg, legend)\\\\n    if grid is None:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    sprites = _build_sprite_queue(key_colors, counts, distractor_color, bg)\\\\n    try:\\\\n        _place_sprites(grid, sprites, bg)\\\\n    except ValueError:\\\\n        return None\\\\n\\\\n    if not np.array_equal(main(grid), expected):\\\\n        return None\\\\n    return grid\\\\n\\\\n\\\\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\\\\n    for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\\\\n        grid = _gen_attempt()\\\\n        if grid is not None:\\\\n            return grid\\\\n    raise RuntimeError(\\\\\\\"failed to generate a valid 58490d8a input\\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8352:- `description`：将网格中每个彩色区域视为投影源，根据其相邻 grey 标记的位置确定投影方向，向对面的墙壁投射该区域的轮廓阴影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8361:  - 投影方向为光源方向的反方向（即阴影投射到光源对面）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8362:  - 从彩色区域中每个像素出发，沿投影方向逐格前进，直到碰到 maroon 墙壁。将墙壁前最后一个 black 像素着色为该区域的颜色。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8363:  - 这些着色像素沿墙壁排列，形成该区域的\\\"轮廓阴影\\\"——即区域在垂直于投影方向的轴上的投影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8364:  - 如果投影路径上遇到其他彩色像素或其阴影，穿过它们继续前进（不被阻挡）。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/codegen_logs_20260618_122116_seed1155420539_gpt54_xhigh/6_4.log:8367:- `Key insight`：解题者需要先建立\\\"grey 标记 = 光源位置\\\"这一映射，再推导出阴影投射到对面墙壁上这一空间关系；最终的阴影不是区域的简单复制，而是区域沿投影方向坍缩到墙壁上的一维轮廓投影。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/17/codegen_prompts/3.md:12:- `description`：利用嵌套同心边框的颜色顺序作为刻度尺，角落的颜色序列量出旋转次数后，将最内层图案旋转输出。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445/17/codegen_prompts/3.md:26:- `Key insight`：嵌套边框的颜色顺序构成一个有序刻度尺，角落的颜色序列在这把尺上量出的跨度才是旋转次数——需要先建立边框的层序映射，再用颜色序列查询跨度，最后执行旋转，形成三层递进推理。\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/6/codegen_prompts/5.md:120:- Full-width horizontal stripes of distinct non-bg colors, stacked vertically.\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed2047415201/6/codegen_prompts/5.md:133:  \\\"src\\\": \\\"horizontal stripes (full-width lines)\\\",\\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed581286445